{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.category==\\\"micro_opt\\\") | {id,title,outcome,fitness,delta_pct,vs_baseline,fmax_mhz,lut4,lesson,changes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"baseline-bench-4ddfa22\",\"title\":\"Baseline retest for cores/bench\",\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":282.82,\"delta_pct\":0.0,\"vs_baseline\":0.0,\"fmax_mhz\":127.03,\"lut4\":9563,\"lesson\":null,\"changes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\",\"title\":\"Fast-path ALU with selective M arithmetic\",\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":406.88,\"delta_pct\":43.87,\"vs_baseline\":43.87,\"fmax_mhz\":182.75,\"lut4\":7513,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.87%): Separating the RV32I fast-path mux from gated M-extension multiply/divide logic, while deriving signed multiply high halves from one unsigned product, can substantially improve CoreMark by removing unconditional arithmetic fanout from ordinary integer and address-generation operations.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Split the ALU into an RV32I fast path and selectively evaluated M-extension arithmetic, preserving real and ALTOPS semantics.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\",\"title\":\"Shared RV32I arithmetic fast path\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":406.88,\"delta_pct\":0.0,\"vs_baseline\":43.87,\"fmax_mhz\":182.75,\"lut4\":7513,\"lesson\":null,\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a shared RV32I add/sub carry chain with compare derivation and a factored fast-path result mux, preserving all M-extension and ALTOPS semantics.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Shared control-flow target adder\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":372.99,\"delta_pct\":-8.33,\"vs_baseline\":31.88,\"fmax_mhz\":167.53,\"lut4\":7520,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -8.33%): Sharing branch/JAL/JALR target arithmetic through a control-gated `target_base` mux and common `target_sum` can worsen CoreMark when the added EX selection and fanout cost more than the removed parallel adders, so arithmetic sharing must be evaluated against its control-path depth.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Fuse branch, JAL, and JALR target formation into one gated PC/rs1 plus immediate adder while preserving redirect and misalignment-trap semantics.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r4s0\",\"title\":\"Direct operand bypass muxing\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"vs_baseline\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"lut4\":null,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 (broken, n/a): Replacing encoded forwarding selects with direct EX/MEM/MEM/WB bypass hits must preserve freshest-writer priority and the forwarded values latched into RVFI source fields, or dependent instructions can expose stale registers and fail `reg_ch0`.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace two-bit forwarding selects with source-use-gated EX/MEM and MEM/WB hit/data bypass signals, preserving freshest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Consume the direct priority bypass values for ALU, branch, and store operands, minimizing the operand mux depth while retaining exact forwarding behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire ID/EX operand values and decoded source-use controls into the direct bypass network without changing the pipeline or RVFI contract.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r5s0\",\"title\":\"Explicit load lane extraction\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":370.39,\"delta_pct\":-8.97,\"vs_baseline\":30.96,\"fmax_mhz\":166.36,\"lut4\":7488,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r5s0 (regression, -8.97%): Replacing variable load shifts with explicit lane-case muxes did not pay off in CoreMark, showing that added MEM-stage selection and routing can outweigh the expected barrel-shifter savings when the existing shift is already synthesized efficiently.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement explicit address-indexed load lane muxes and constant byte-mask cases, preserving exact RV32I load semantics, traps, handshakes, and RVFI fields.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r6s0\",\"title\":\"Source-use-aware load-use interlock\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"vs_baseline\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"lut4\":null,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (broken, n/a): Decode-derived `use_rs1`/`use_rs2` masks make load-use interlocks correctness-critical—any mismatch with the legal instruction decode or IF/ID timing can miss a required bubble and corrupt architectural register state, which `reg_ch0` catches.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose decode-derived use_rs1/use_rs2 signals for the current IF/ID instruction, asserting them only for valid RV32IM consumers.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Gate load-use comparisons with the source-use signals while retaining exact load, x0, redirect, instruction-stall, and data-stall precedence.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the ID-stage source-use metadata into hazard detection without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\",\"title\":\"Consumer-specific EX operand mux factoring\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":368.01,\"delta_pct\":-9.55,\"vs_baseline\":30.12,\"fmax_mhz\":165.29,\"lut4\":7611,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (regression, -9.55%): Consumer-specific EX operand factoring can regress CoreMark when it duplicates the `fwd_rs1_sel`/`fwd_rs2_sel` mux trees for ALU inputs alongside canonical forwarded operands, so shortening nominal immediate/PC paths must be weighed against added mux replication and routing fanout.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Refactor ALU operand selection so immediate and PC consumers bypass irrelevant forwarding mux levels while branches, stores, JALR, and RVFI retain exact forwarded operands.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\",\"title\":\"Predecoded class/sub-op ALU control\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":318.29,\"delta_pct\":-21.77,\"vs_baseline\":12.54,\"fmax_mhz\":142.96,\"lut4\":7468,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r8s0 (regression, -21.77%): Predecoding ALU class/sub-operation fields did not pay off when the added ID/EX control fields and fanout outweighed removing EX range comparisons, showing that narrower control encoding helps only if it also reduces physical routing on the common CoreMark path.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add compact predecoded ALU class/sub-operation fields to the pipeline control bundle while retaining all existing trap and memory controls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/decoder.sv\",\"description\":\"Generate the explicit M-class and compact ALU sub-operation controls only inside validated RV32IM opcode/funct matches, preserving strict illegal defaults.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the predecoded ALU class/sub-operation controls into ID/EX without changing operand, hazard, or RVFI metadata timing.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Use the predecoded class/sub-operation selects to bypass 5-bit range/equality decoding on the common RV32I path while preserving real M arithmetic and ALTOPS semantics.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r9s0\",\"title\":\"Bit-factored M-extension ALU gating\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":179.41,\"delta_pct\":-55.91,\"vs_baseline\":-36.56,\"fmax_mhz\":80.58,\"lut4\":7470,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r9s0 (regression, -55.91%): Bit-factoring M-operation and multiply/divide predicates can regress even as it removes relational compares, showing that decode Boolean simplification is not a proxy for a shorter synthesized control-to-result path or lower fanout.\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Factor the existing ALU M-operation and divide gating predicates into Boolean decode from the current operation encoding, preserving real RV32M and ALTOPS behavior while reducing common-path range-comparator logic.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
