{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml\\\")[\\\"id\\\"]'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Reuse ALU subtract flags for branches\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current EX stage has a shared branch subtract, while the ALU also\n  computes an independent result cone for the same forwarded operands. The\n  successful branch-flag optimization shows that this compare network is\n  timing-relevant, and CoreMark executes enough branches for duplicated\n  subtract logic and routing to affect Fmax.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make branch decode select the ALU subtract operation and expose the\n  subtract result flags (zero, unsigned borrow, and overflow-corrected signed\n  less-than) from the ALU. Replace the separate EX branch-difference logic\n  with those flags, allowing the ALU's existing fast-path subtract carry\n  chain to serve both its result and all branch predicates. Keep branch\n  target arithmetic, forwarding, misalignment traps, RVFI metadata, and\n  RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior unchanged. This preserves IPC and may reduce\n  duplicated arithmetic/routing on the branch redirect path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Expose shared subtract zero, borrow, and signed-less-than flags alongside the existing RV32I fast-path result, preserving real and ALTOPS M-extension behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Set the validated conditional-branch control to use the ALU subtract operation without changing branch legality or operands.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume ALU-provided compare flags for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU and remove the duplicate EX branch subtract cone while retaining redirect and trap semantics.\"\n\"hyp-20260710-001-r11s0\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
