ng valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 374.56, \"delta_pct\": -7.94, \"vs_baseline\": 32.44, \"fmax_mhz\": 166.97, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4457730, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7622, \"ff\": 1870, \"seeds\": [172.47, 166.97, 160.49], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T21:18:00.493070Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -7.94%): On a single-ported dmem, a one-entry store buffer can lose to its own store-priority arbitration, address-conflict checks, and MEM-stage load-forward path, whose control and conservative ordering stalls outweigh the store bubbles they hide in CoreMark.\"}\n13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny fully tagged last-target predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Taken-loop redirects are still paid in EX, but the earlier BTFNT and RAS\\nexperiments showed that fetch-time instruction decoding and speculative\\nstack bookkeeping can cost more timing and area than they save. A single\\nfully tagged entry can learn the hot target of the most recently taken\\ncontrol-transfer PC with substantially less state and no dependence on\\nimemData in the fetch critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Taken-loop redirects are still paid in EX, but the earlier BTFNT and RAS\\nexperiments showed that fetch-time instruction decoding and speculative\\nstack bookkeeping can cost more timing and area than they save. A single\\nfully tagged entry can learn the hot target of the most recently taken\\ncontrol-transfer PC with substantially less state and no dependence on\\nimemData in the fetch critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry last-target branch buffer indexed by an exact full-PC tag.\\nOn a hit, fetch advances directly to the recorded target while the\\ncurrent instruction carries prediction-valid and predicted-next-PC bits\\nthrough ID/EX. Train the entry only from a valid EX-resolved taken branch,\\nJAL, or JALR; invalidate it when a matching conditional branch resolves\\nnot-taken. EX compares the carried prediction with the resolved next PC,\\nsuppressing the normal redirect on a hit and redirecting plus flushing on\\nevery miss. This preserves precise RVFI pc_wdata and recovery while\\navoiding fetch-time opcode/immediate decode and limiting predictor muxing\\nto one tag compare and target mux.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the one-entry fully tagged last-target buffer, including exact-PC lookup, taken-transfer training, matching not-taken invalidation, and reset state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Give fetch a predicted target input with imemReady and EX-redirect priority, advancing on a valid predictor hit without flushing the currently fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the decoded instruction without altering decoder legality or register operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare predicted next PC against the resolved branch/jump next PC, generate redirects only for misses or unpredicted transfers, and retain precise misalignment-trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the predictor lookup/training path, coordinate predictor-hit and EX-mispredict control with existing flushes, and preserve RVFI retirement ordering.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\"