{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r12s0.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r12s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r12s0\ntitle: \"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage pipeline currently inserts a full bubble whenever the\n  instruction immediately after a load consumes its result, even though the\n  combinational MEM-stage load extraction already has the returned word in\n  the same cycle. CoreMark has a dense mix of loads followed by address,\n  compare, and loop-body operations, so these conservative interlocks reduce\n  retired instructions per cycle independently of Fmax.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a precise MEM-to-EX load-result bypass that forwards the sign- or\n  zero-extended load value directly from mem_stage into the EX operand mux.\n  Suppress the load-use bubble only when the load response is ready and the\n  access is legal; retain the existing stall when dmemReady is low and retain\n  normal trap behavior for misaligned loads. Give this bypass priority over\n  MEM/WB forwarding, carry the forwarded operands into the existing EX/MEM\n  RVFI fields, and leave retirement order, memory masks, and all RV32M paths\n  unchanged. This should improve CoreMark IPC without adding a new pipeline\n  stage or speculative state.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the already-computed load extraction result and a legal-load forward-valid signal without changing dmem handshakes, alignment traps, or RVFI capture.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a highest-priority MEM load-data forwarding selection while retaining freshest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the MEM load bypass in the EX operand muxes and latch the resulting operands for architectural execution and RVFI source data.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate only the load-use bubble on the legal, ready MEM bypass; continue freezing the pipeline for dmem stalls and trapping accesses.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire mem_stage load-forward data and validity through forwarding and hazard control while preserving the single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
