{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r13s0.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r13s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Narrow post-EX control payload\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage core carries the full decode control record through both\n  EX/MEM and MEM/WB even though ALU selection, branch classification, and\n  jump classification are no longer consumed after EX. Those dead fields add\n  flip-flops, routing, and control fanout around the common memory and\n  writeback paths, where an IPC-neutral timing improvement is especially\n  valuable on the small Tang Nano device.\nhypothesis: |\n  Introduce a compact post-EX memory/writeback control record containing only\n  memory read/write, width/sign extension, register-write, load-select, and\n  illegal/trap bits. Pack this reduced record into EX/MEM and MEM/WB while\n  mapping the existing decoded controls into it at the EX boundary. Keep all\n  EX branch, jump, ALU, and forwarding behavior unchanged, and preserve the\n  exact memory masks, misalignment traps, RVFI fields, writeback selection,\n  and single-cycle retirement semantics. Removing the unused control-flow\n  fields from the broad pipeline bundles should reduce post-EX routing and\n  improve Fmax without adding bubbles or speculative state.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact post-EX memory/writeback control typedef and use it in EX/MEM and MEM/WB instead of carrying the full decode control record.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Translate the validated EX control record into the reduced post-EX control fields while preserving jump results, misalignment traps, and all existing forwarding and retirement metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume and pipeline the reduced control record without changing dmem handshakes, byte masks, load extension, RVFI reporting, or writeback behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
