et the high-value JALR-return case\\nwithout adding instruction decode and target arithmetic to IF.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small speculative return-address stack and perform return prediction\\nin ID for canonical JALR returns (x1/x5 link register, zero immediate).\\nTrack call pushes and return pops with a shadow/speculative stack, carry an\\nexplicit predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid bit through the pipeline,\\nand compare the prediction with EX's resolved next PC. On a mismatch, EX\\nmust redirect and restore the stack metadata so RVFI pc_wdata, ordering,\\ntraps, and arbitrary symbolic instruction streams remain precise. Keeping\\nthe lookup in ID confines the added muxing to the existing decode path while\\nremoving return redirect bubbles on repeated CoreMark call sites.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and return-stack action metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize canonical calls and returns, query the small return-address stack in decode, and pipeline prediction metadata without changing the architectural decode legality defaults.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept an early decode-stage predicted target with correct priority relative to reset, bus stalls, and EX recovery redirects, while retaining sequential fetch when the stack has no valid entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the carried return prediction against the resolved JAL/JALR next PC, generate precise recovery redirects, and expose committed call/return outcomes for stack repair.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode prediction and resolved recovery/training signals through the pipeline so only correctly predicted returns avoid the existing EX redirect flush.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {