{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.yaml && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Shared control-flow target adder\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The successful ALU optimization showed that redundant arithmetic cones on\n  the common EX path materially limit Tang Nano 20K Fmax.  The current EX\n  stage independently computes pc+imm for branches and JAL and rs1+imm for\n  JALR, even though only one control-flow target is needed for an instruction.\n  Those parallel adders and the following mux add fanout to the same stage\n  without improving ordinary integer throughput.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the separate branch-target adder and JALR adder with one\n  control-gated target adder whose base is selected between PC and forwarded\n  rs1.  Reuse its result for both branch and jump target formation, retaining\n  JALR bit-zero clearing, misaligned-target trapping, redirect priority, and\n  the existing RVFI pc_next behavior.  This should reduce EX arithmetic area\n  and control-to-target mux depth while leaving the retirement schedule and\n  CoreMark IPC unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Fuse branch, JAL, and JALR target formation into one gated PC/rs1 plus immediate adder while preserving redirect and misalignment-trap semantics.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\", \"title\"=>\"Shared control-flow target adder\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The successful ALU optimization showed that redundant arithmetic cones on\\nthe common EX path materially limit Tang Nano 20K Fmax.  The current EX\\nstage independently computes pc+imm for branches and JAL and rs1+imm for\\nJALR, even though only one control-flow target is needed for an instruction.\\nThose parallel adders and the following mux add fanout to the same stage\\nwithout improving ordinary integer throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Replace the separate branch-target adder and JALR adder with one\\ncontrol-gated target adder whose base is selected between PC and forwarded\\nrs1.  Reuse its result for both branch and jump target formation, retaining\\nJALR bit-zero clearing, misaligned-target trapping, redirect priority, and\\nthe existing RVFI pc_next behavior.  This should reduce EX arithmetic area\\nand control-to-target mux depth while leaving the retirement schedule and\\nCoreMark IPC unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>3, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Fuse branch, JAL, and JALR target formation into one gated PC/rs1 plus immediate adder while preserving redirect and misalignment-trap semantics.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
