an unresolved producer. Use\\nthe early redirect to flush just the younger fetch work, while carrying the\\nresolved next-PC and misalignment-trap metadata into retirement so RVFI,\\nordering, and illegal-instruction behavior remain unchanged. Removing the\\nbranch comparator/target path from EX should reduce taken-loop bubbles\\nwithout putting instruction decode or target formation on the IF critical\\npath.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with resolved next-PC and control-transfer fault metadata needed for precise RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment traps.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve legal branches, JAL, and JALR in ID using dedicated target/compare logic and explicit operand bypass inputs, while exporting an early redirect and trap decision.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Prioritize the ID-stage redirect over sequential fetch, coordinate one-cycle flushes with the existing EX and dmem-stall controls, and wire resolved next-PC data to retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage dependency checks so branches and JALR wait for unavailable load results while allowing EX/MEM and MEM/WB ALU results to bypass into ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the ID-resolved transfer metadata, retain a precise fallback for malformed or misaligned transfers, and remove redundant EX control-transfer work from the timing-critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with resolved next-PC and control-transfer fault metadata needed for precise RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment traps.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve legal branches, JAL, and JALR in ID using 