{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.yaml; rg -n '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-[0-9]+-r4s[0-9]\\\"|hyp-20260710-001-r4s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r4s0.log | tail -n 40\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Single-entry nonblocking store buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage pipeline freezes globally whenever an EX/MEM store\n  sees io_dmemReady low, even though a store has no result that younger ALU\n  instructions need. The prior general completion-queue attempt failed\n  liveness, so a bounded store-only structure is a lower-risk way to overlap\n  the benchmark's random data-bus stalls without introducing broad out-of-order\n  retirement machinery.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry FIFO store buffer at the MEM boundary. A store is accepted\n  into the buffer and retires in program order, while the buffer independently\n  holds its address, byte mask, and replicated write data until io_dmemReady\n  acknowledges the write. Allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed\n  behind a buffered store; keep younger loads ordered by stalling them on a\n  possible store-buffer address conflict, and stop the front end only when the\n  buffer is full or an older memory-order condition requires it. Keep loads,\n  RVFI fields, redirects, and trap handling on the existing precise path so\n  this structural change primarily removes store-induced global bubbles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\"\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r4s0.log:13:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'ls -la cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses 2>/dev/null || true'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"total 1504\\ndrwxr-xr-x  25 bonetto  staff     800 Jul 10 18:00 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x   7 bonetto  staff     224 Jul 10 17:59 ..\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff     314 Jul 10 16:52 .agent.hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.last\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff    6553 Jul 10 16:52 .agent.hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.log\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff     284 Jul 10 17:14 .agent.hyp-20260710-001-r2s0.last\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff   83792 Jul 10 17:14 .agent.hyp-20260710-001-r2s0.log\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff     263 Jul 10 17:39 .agent.hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.last\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff  103705 Jul 10 17:39 .agent.hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.log\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff   72485 Jul 10 17:59 .agent.hyp-20260710-001-r4s0.log\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff     288 Jul 10 16:52 .agent.hyp-20260710-002-r1s1.last\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff   56517 Jul 10 16:52 .agent.hyp-20260710-002-r1s1.log\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff     373 Jul 10 17:14 .agent.hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.last\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff   14767 Jul 10 17:14 .agent.hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.log\\n-rw-r--r--   1 bonetto  staff     330 Jul 10 17:39 .agent.hyp