k, and replicated write data until io_dmemReady\\\\nacknowledges the write. Allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed\\\\nbehind a buffered store; keep younger loads ordered by stalling them on a\\\\npossible store-buffer address conflict, and stop the front end only when the\\\\nbuffer is full or an older memory-order condition requires it. Keep loads,\\\\nRVFI fields, redirects, and trap handling on the existing precise path so\\\\nthis structural change primarily removes store-induced global bubbles.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": 