tions, prose, or anything other than the bullet line.\\\\\\\\n']' returned non-zero exit status 1.\\\"}\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:7:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"PC-indexed learned branch target buffer\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The previous static BTFNT predictor put branch decode, immediate formation,\\\\ntarget addition, and prediction metadata directly on the instruction-fetch\\\\npath, reducing Fmax enough to erase its control-flow benefit. CoreMark still\\\\nhas repeated loop branches whose targets can be learned after the first\\\\niteration, so prediction should be driven by the fetch PC rather than by\\\\ncombinational decoding of every fetched instruction.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The previous static BTFNT predictor put branch decode, immediate formation,\\\\ntarget addition, and prediction metadata directly on the instruction-fetch\\\\npath, reducing Fmax enough to erase its control-flow benefit. CoreMark still\\\\nhas repeated loop branches whose targets can be learned after the first\\\\niteration, so prediction should be driven by the fetch PC rather than by\\\\ncombinational decoding of every fetched instruction.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a tiny direct-mapped BTB with PC tags, cached branch targets, and a\\\\ntwo-bit taken counter. A tagged hit in IF predicts the cached target using\\\\nonly the current PC, keeping opcode/funct/immediate decode out of the IF\\\\ncritical path. Carry the predicted next PC with the instruction; in EX,\\\\ncompare it with the resolved branch next PC and redirect only on a\\\\nmisprediction. Train the BTB from resolved conditional branches, saturating\\\\ntoward taken or not-taken, while retaining precise flush, trap, RVFI, and\\\\nload/store stall behavior. This should remove repeated taken-loop redirect\\\\nbubbles without repeating the timing-costly fetch-time BTFNT logic.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a small tagged BTB with two-bit direction counters, PC-only lookup, redirect recovery, and resolved-branch training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the BTB prediction metadata alongside the instruction and decoded operands.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Resolve the actual branch next PC and assert redirect only when it differs from the carried prediction, preserving misalignment traps.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire resolved conditional-branch PC, target, and outcome back to IF for BTB training while preserving existing hazard and RVFI control.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a small tagged BTB with two-bit direction counters, PC-only lookup, redirect recovery, and resolved-branch training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the BTB prediction metadata alongside the instruction and decoded operands.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Resolve the actual branch next PC and assert redirect only when it differs from the carried prediction, preserving misalignment traps.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire resolved conditional-branch PC, target, and outcome back to IF for BTB tr