{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r7s0.yaml; ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r7s0.yaml; git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r7s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Consumer-specific EX operand mux factoring\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The optimized core still builds fully forwarded rs1/rs2 operands before\n  applying the EX-stage PC/immediate selection. For common ADDI and memory\n  address operations, that leaves an unnecessary forwarding mux on the ALU\n  input even though the instruction cannot use the forwarded value there.\n  The prior ALU optimization improved Fmax without changing IPC, so removing\n  another level of common execute-path muxing is a promising low-risk follow-up.\nhypothesis: |\n  Factor the EX operand network by consumer: select the immediate directly as\n  the ALU B operand when alu_src is set, and select PC directly as the ALU A\n  operand for AUIPC, while retaining the existing freshest-writer forwarding\n  muxes for branch comparisons, stores, JALR, and RVFI source values. This\n  should shorten the dominant address-generation and integer ALU paths and\n  reduce forwarding-control fanout without adding latency, changing hazards,\n  or changing any architectural result or retirement metadata.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Refactor ALU operand selection so immediate and PC consumers bypass irrelevant forwarding mux levels while branches, stores, JALR, and RVFI retain exact forwarded operands.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\", \"title\"=>\"Consumer-specific EX operand mux factoring\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The optimized core still builds fully forwarded rs1/rs2 operands before\\napplying the EX-stage PC/immediate selection. For common ADDI and memory\\naddress operations, that leaves an unnecessary forwarding mux on the ALU\\ninput even though the instruction cannot use the forwarded value there.\\nThe prior ALU optimization improved Fmax without changing IPC, so removing\\nanother level of common execute-path muxing is a promising low-risk follow-up.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Factor the EX operand network by consumer: select the immediate directly as\\nthe ALU B operand when alu_src is set, and select PC directly as the ALU A\\noperand for AUIPC, while retaining the existing freshest-writer forwarding\\nmuxes for branch comparisons, stores, JALR, and RVFI source values. This\\nshould shorten the dominant address-generation and integer ALU paths and\\nreduce forwarding-control fanout without adding latency, changing hazards,\\nor changing any architectural result or retirement metadata.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>3, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Refactor ALU operand selection so immediate and PC consumers bypass irrelevant forwarding mux levels while branches, stores, JALR, and RVFI retain exact forwarded operands.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
