lative stack, carry an\\nexplicit predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid bit through the pipeline,\\nand compare the prediction with EX's resolved next PC. On a mismatch, EX\\nmust redirect and restore the stack metadata so RVFI pc_wdata, ordering,\\ntraps, and arbitrary symbolic instruction streams remain precise. Keeping\\nthe lookup in ID confines the added muxing to the existing decode path while\\nremoving return redirect bubbles on repeated CoreMark call sites.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and return-stack action metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize canonical calls and returns, query the small return-address stack in decode, and pipeline prediction metadata without changing the architectural decode legality defaults.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept an early decode-stage predicted target with correct priority relative to reset, bus stalls, and EX recovery redirects, while retaining sequential fetch when the stack has no valid entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the carried return prediction against the resolved JAL/JALR next PC, generate precise recovery redirects, and expose committed call/return outcomes for stack repair.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode prediction and resolved recovery/training signals through the pipeline so only correctly predicted returns avoid the existing EX redirect flush.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and return-stack action metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize canonical calls and returns, query the small return-address stack in decode, and pipeline prediction metadata without changing the architectural decode legality defaults.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept an early decode-stage predicted target with correct priority relative to reset, bus stalls, and EX recovery redirects, while retaining sequential fetch when the stack has no valid entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the carried return prediction against the resolved JAL/JALR next PC, generate precise recovery redirects, and expose committed call/return outcomes for stack repair.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode prediction and resolved recovery/training signals through the pipeline so only correctly predicted returns avoid the existing EX redirect flush.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 147.68, \"delta_pct\": -63.7, \"vs_baseline\": -47.78, \"fmax_mhz\": 66.33, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8424, \"ff\": 2164, \"seeds\": [63.25, 66.89, 66.33], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T20:57:07.071453Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r3s2 (regression, -63.70%): Decode-stage RAS prediction can lose badly when speculative push/pop checkpoints, recovery control, and carried predicted-PC metadata add ID/EX/EX muxing and fanout that cost more than the saved JALR return flushes in CoreMark.\"}\n11:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Direct operand bypass muxing\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The successful ALU optimization has removed the largest unconditional\\narithmetic cone, leaving the EX operand path as a likely next limiter.\\nForwarding currently performs register comparisons, encodes the result as\\na two-bit select, and then decodes that select through a 32-bit mux for each\\noperand.  CoreMark's dependent integer and address-generation instructions\\nexercise this path frequently.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The successful ALU optimization has removed the largest unconditional\\narithmetic cone, leaving the EX operand path as a likely next limiter.\\nForwarding currently performs register comparisons, encodes the result as\\na two-bit select, and then decodes that select through a 32-bit mux for each\\noperand.  CoreMark's dependent integer and address-generation instructions\\nexercise this path frequently.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the encoded forwarding selects with a direct, priority-ordered\\noperand bypass network.  Generate EX/MEM and MEM/WB hit terms beside the\\nregister-number comparisons, gate comparisons for operands unused by the\\ndecoded instruction, and select the freshest 32-bit value with shallow\\ncascaded muxes in EX.  Preserve EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority, x0 behavior,\\nload-use stalling, branch/store operand values, and all RVFI-visible source\\ndata.  Removing the select encode/decode layer should shorten the common\\ndependency-to-ALU path and reduce control fanout without changing IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace two-bit forwarding selects with source-use-gated EX/MEM and MEM/WB hit/data bypass signals, preserving freshest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the direct priority bypass values for ALU, branch, and store operands, minimizing the operand mux depth while retaining exact forwarding behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire ID/EX operand values and decoded source-use controls into the direct bypass network without changing the pipeline or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace two-bit forwarding selects with source-use-gated EX/MEM and MEM/WB hit/data bypass signals, preserving freshest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the direct priority bypass values for ALU, branch, and store operands, minimizing the operand mux depth while retaining exact forwarding behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire ID/EX operand values and decoded source-use controls into the direct bypass network without changing the pipeline or RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\ncd\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:21  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:21  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:21  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:21  Status: failed\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:21 (21)\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:12 (12)\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 step 20\\nSBY 18:09:34 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: reg_ch0\\n\\n--- reg_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 18:09:13 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 9..\\nSBY 18:09:13 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 10..\\nSBY 18:09:14 [reg_ch0