reserving exact RV32I load semantics, traps, handshakes, and RVFI fields.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement explicit address-indexed load lane muxes and constant byte-mask cases, preserving exact RV32I load semantics, traps, handshakes, and RVFI fields.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 370.39, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -8.97, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 30.96, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 166.36, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7488, \\\"ff\\\": 1858, \\\"seeds\\\": [165.84, 173.04, 166.36], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T21:29:22.464159Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 5, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r5s0 (regression, -8.97%): Replacing variable load shifts with explicit lane-case muxes did not pay off in CoreMark, showing that added MEM-stage selection and routing can outweigh the expected barrel-shifter savings when the existing shift is already synthesized efficiently.\\\"}\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:15:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Retimed two-stage execute pipeline\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline places operand forwarding, a 32-bit ALU,\\\\nbranch comparison, and control-transfer target formation in one EX cycle.\\\\nThat wide fan-in and arithmetic cone is a likely remaining Fmax limiter\\\\nafter the fast-path ALU optimization, while the prior buffering attempts\\\\nshow that adding queues can cost more IPC than they recover.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline places operand forwarding, a 32-bit ALU,\\\\nbranch comparison, and control-transfer target formation in one EX cycle.\\\\nThat wide fan-in and arithmetic cone is a likely remaining Fmax limiter\\\\nafter the fast-path ALU optimization, while the prior buffering attempts\\\\nshow that adding queues can cost more IPC than they recover.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Split EX into EX1 and EX2 with a pipeline register between operand\\\\nselection and execution. EX1 performs source-use-aware forwarding and\\\\ncaptures the resolved operands and control metadata; EX2 performs the ALU,\\\\nbranch compare/target calculation, and memory-address generation before the\\\\nexisting MEM boundary. Add explicit EX1/EX2 bypass priority and interlocks\\\\nfor the extra latency, and keep redirects, load-use behavior, dmem stalls,\\\\nand RVFI payloads tied to the same in-order instruction. The added stage\\\\nshould shorten the critical operand-to-result path enough to raise Fmax\\\\nwithout the area and ordering overhead of speculative queues.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend the pipeline bundle definitions with an EX1/EX2 execution payload carrying forwarded operands, control, and RVFI metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Restructure execute into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/branch/address EX2 stages, with precise redirect and misalignment-trap propagation.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add freshest-writer bypass selection for the retimed EX1/EX2 boundary while preserving load suppression, x0 handling, and EX/MEM priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add the one-cycle interlocks and flush/stall precedence required by the extra execute stage, including dmem backpressure and redirect recovery.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the retimed execute stages into MEM/WB, forwarding, hazard control, and RVFI retirement without changing the single-channel top-level contract.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Extend the pipeline bundle definitions with an EX1/EX2 execution payload carrying forwarded operands, control, and RVFI metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Restructure execute into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/branch/address EX2 stages, with precise redirect and misalignment-trap propagation.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add freshest-writer bypass selection for the retimed EX1/EX2 boundary while preserving load suppression, x0 handling, and EX/MEM priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add the one-cycle interlocks and flush/stall precedence required by the extra execute stage, including dmem backpressure and redirect recovery.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the retimed execute stages into MEM/WB, forwarding, hazard control, and RVFI retirement without changing the single-channel top-level contract.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 188.61, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -53.64, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -33.31, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 102.76, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 5448270, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7636, \\\"ff\\\": 2112, \\\"seeds\\\": [88.33, 110.57, 102.76], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T21:43:14.515659Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 5, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -53.64%): Retiming EX into EX1/EX2 made dependency, redirect, and dmem-stall interlo