{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r8s0.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r8s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\ntitle: \"Predecoded class/sub-op ALU control\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current routed critical path starts at an ID/EX ALU-control bit and\n  traverses the execute ALU's 5-bit operation decode before reaching the\n  ordinary RV32I result and carry-chain logic.  The successful ALU fast-path\n  change removed the large M-extension cone, so reducing control decode and\n  mux depth on this remaining common path is a focused next opportunity.\nhypothesis: |\n  Predecode the ALU control in ID into an explicit M-extension class bit and\n  compact RV32I/M sub-operation fields, then pipeline those fields instead of\n  making EX rediscover operation classes with range comparisons and a broad\n  5-bit case select.  Implement the RV32I fast path with direct class/sub-op\n  selects and keep the existing isolated multiply/divide path behind the M\n  bit.  Preserve every RV32I and RV32M result, RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior,\n  illegal-instruction handling, forwarding, and the unchanged single-cycle\n  execute/retirement schedule.  The expected gain is lower control-to-ALU\n  delay and reduced control fanout with no IPC cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact predecoded ALU class/sub-operation fields to the pipeline control bundle while retaining all existing trap and memory controls.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Generate the explicit M-class and compact ALU sub-operation controls only inside validated RV32IM opcode/funct matches, preserving strict illegal defaults.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predecoded ALU class/sub-operation controls into ID/EX without changing operand, hazard, or RVFI metadata timing.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Use the predecoded class/sub-operation selects to bypass 5-bit range/equality decoding on the common RV32I path while preserving real M arithmetic and ALTOPS semantics.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
