rough ID/EX. Train the entry only from a valid EX-resolved taken branch,\\nJAL, or JALR; invalidate it when a matching conditional branch resolves\\nnot-taken. EX compares the carried prediction with the resolved next PC,\\nsuppressing the normal redirect on a hit and redirecting plus flushing on\\nevery miss. This preserves precise RVFI pc_wdata and recovery while\\navoiding fetch-time opcode/immediate decode and limiting predictor muxing\\nto one tag compare and target mux.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the one-entry fully tagged last-target buffer, including exact-PC lookup, taken-transfer training, matching not-taken invalidation, and reset state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Give fetch a predicted target input with imemReady and EX-redirect priority, advancing on a valid predictor hit without flushing the currently fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the decoded instruction without altering decoder legality or register operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare predicted next PC against the resolved branch/jump next PC, generate redirects only for misses or unpredicted transfers, and retain precise misalignment-trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the predictor lookup/training path, coordinate predictor-hit and EX-mispredict control with existing flushes, and preserve RVFI retirement ordering.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.s