{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis,changes,outcome,fitness,delta_pct,implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\",\"title\":\"Elastic in-order data-memory completion queue\",\"motivation\":\"The current MEM-stage handshake freezes PC, ID/EX, and EX/MEM whenever\\nio_dmemReady is low, so a transient data-bus stall blocks unrelated ALU\\ninstructions and directly lowers CoreMark instructions per cycle. The\\nrecent fetch FIFO result also shows that buffering only the front end is\\ninsufficient when the dominant stall is downstream.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current MEM-stage handshake freezes PC, ID/EX, and EX/MEM whenever\\nio_dmemReady is low, so a transient data-bus stall blocks unrelated ALU\\ninstructions and directly lowers CoreMark instructions per cycle. The\\nrecent fetch FIFO result also shows that buffering only the front end is\\ninsufficient when the dominant stall is downstream.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Restructure the memory boundary as a small elastic in-order queue with a\\ndedicated completion/retirement head. Allow younger independent ALU\\ninstructions to execute into queue entries while an older load or store\\nwaits for io_dmemReady, but prevent younger memory operations from passing\\nan older memory operation and hold dependent consumers until the load data\\nis available. Retire only the queue head, preserving RVFI order, precise\\ntraps, register writeback, and architectural memory ordering. This should\\noverlap random dmem backpressure with useful integer work without adding a\\nfetch-time critical path or changing the external bus contract.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":8,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the metadata needed for elastic memory/completion entries, including age, completion, and deferred load/store state while preserving the existing RVFI payload.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single blocking MEM/WB boundary with a small in-order memory/completion queue that holds stalled data requests, accepts younger non-memory results, and exposes only the oldest completed entry to writeback and RVFI.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Generate queue-full, older-memory-order, and load-result dependency stalls instead of freezing the complete pipeline on every dmemReady low cycle.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire elastic queue ready/valid flow through EX, MEM, WB, and retirement so dmem backpressure overlaps independent execution while redirects and RVFI remain precise.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the metadata needed for elastic memory/completion entries, including age, completion, and deferred load/store state while preserving the existing RVFI payload.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single blocking MEM/WB boundary with a small in-order memory/completion queue that holds stalled data requests, accepts younger non-memory results, and exposes only the oldest completed entry to writeback and RVFI.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Generate queue-full, older-memory-order, and load-result dependency stalls instead of freezing the complete pipeline on every dmemReady low cycle.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire elastic queue ready/valid flow through EX, MEM, WB, and retirement so dmem backpressure overlaps independent execution while redirects and RVFI remain precise.\"}],\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\",\"title\":\"Constrained ALU completion skid during data stalls\",\"motivation\":\"A dmemReady stall currently freezes the entire five-stage machine even when\\nthe instruction behind the blocked load or store is an independent integer\\noperation. The earlier full elastic-memory queue was too broad and failed\\nliveness, while a store-only buffer added arbitration and ordering cost. A\\nmuch narrower completion structure can recover some of the lost overlap\\nwithout speculating or reordering any memory operation.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"A dmemReady stall currently freezes the entire five-stage machine even when\\nthe instruction behind the blocked load or store is an independent integer\\noperation. The earlier full elastic-memory queue was too broad and failed\\nliveness, while a store-only buffer added arbitration and ordering cost. A\\nmuch narrower completion structure can recover some of the lost overlap\\nwithout speculating or reordering any memory operation.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a one-entry in-order completion skid between EX and MEM that accepts only\\nyounger, non-memory, non-control ALU instructions while an older EX/MEM load\\nor store waits for io_dmemReady. Keep the blocked memory operation as the\\nretirement head, forbid younger loads, stores, branches, jumps, and illegal\\noperations from entering the skid, and stop the front end once the skid is\\nfull. After the memory completes, drain the skid entry into the normal\\nMEM/WB path before accepting another result. Add explicit forwarding from\\nthe skid entry and preserve age ordering, precise redirects, RVFI source\\nvalues, and register writeback. This limited bypass should hide short random\\ndmem stalls with modest area and control overhead while avoiding the timing\\nand correctness risks of a general completion queue.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define a compact completion-skid payload and valid/age metadata for a younger ALU result while retaining the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the one-entry ALU skid between EX and MEM, select the oldest completed result for writeback, and connect skid forwarding without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose a sideband candidate for non-memory, non-control ALU instructions and prevent skid capture of operations that could redirect, trap, or access memory.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add ordered drain/capture behavior so a blocked older data request remains the retirement head and the younger ALU completion reaches MEM/WB only after it.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace unconditional dmem-stall freezing with skid-full and dependency-aware backpressure, while keeping memory ordering, load-use hazards, redirect flushes, and forward progress precise.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Give the completion skid highest forwarding priority for dependent ALU operands, with x0 and valid gating and older EX/MEM/MEM/WB priority preserved when the skid is absent.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define a compact completion-skid payload and valid/age metadata for a younger ALU result while retaining the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the one-entry ALU skid between EX and MEM, select the oldest completed result for writeback, and connect skid forwarding without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose a sideband candidate for non-memory, non-control ALU instructions and prevent skid capture of operations that could redirect, trap, or access memory.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add ordered drain/capture behavior so a blocked older data request remains the retirement head and the younger ALU completion reaches MEM/WB only after it.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace unconditional dmem-stall freezing with skid-full and dependency-aware backpressure, while keeping memory ordering, load-use hazards, redirect flushes, and forward progress precise.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Give the completion skid highest forwarding priority for dependent ALU operands, with x0 and valid gating and older EX/MEM/MEM/WB priority preserved when the skid is absent.\"}],\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\",\"title\":\"Stage-local micro-op pipeline records\",\"motivation\":\"The five-stage datapath currently carries the full control bundle through\\nevery pipeline boundary, including branch, memory, execute, and retirement\\nfields that are irrelevant to most downstream stages. That creates broad\\ncontrol fanout and routing across the EX/MEM and MEM/WB boundaries even\\nthough CoreMark is dominated by ordinary ALU and address-generation ops.\\nThe prior structural attempts that added queues or pipeline stages paid\\nsubstantial control and latency cost; a same-depth restructuring can target\\nFmax without adding retirement or dependency latency.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The five-stage datapath currently carries the full control bundle through\\nevery pipeline boundary, including branch, memory, execute, and retirement\\nfields that are irrelevant to most downstream stages. That creates broad\\ncontrol fanout and routing across the EX/MEM and MEM/WB boundaries even\\nthough CoreMark is dominated by ordinary ALU and address-generation ops.\\nThe prior structural attempts that added queues or pipeline stages paid\\nsubstantial control and latency cost; a same-depth restructuring can target\\nFmax without adding retirement or dependency latency.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Partition the pipeline record into stage-local micro-op controls and a\\nseparate retirement metadata payload. Decode still validates the complete\\nRV32IM instruction, but ID/EX latches only execute-relevant controls and\\noperands; EX/MEM forwards only memory/writeback controls plus the RVFI\\nfields needed after execution; and MEM/WB carries only memory-result and\\nretirement state. Remove redundant branch-target bookkeeping and unused\\ncontrol fields from later records, while preserving valid/flush behavior,\\nforwarded source values, precise trap and misalignment metadata, and every\\nRVFI field at the existing single retirement boundary. Narrower stage-local\\nfanout should improve routed Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the monolithic control propagation with compact execute, memory, writeback, and retirement pipeline record types that retain all required RVFI metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/decoder.sv\",\"description\":\"Keep the strict legal-instruction decode but expose stage-local control fields instead of requiring the full control bundle to cross every stage.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the compact execute micro-op, operands, immediate, register addresses, and precise retirement metadata at the ID/EX boundary.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Consume the execute-local record and emit only the memory/writeback controls, computed result, and retirement metadata needed by later stages.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Use a memory-local record and produce a narrow MEM/WB retirement record, preserving alignment traps, byte masks, load data, and RVFI values.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Reconnect the stage-local records and forwarding/control wiring without changing the top-level IO, single-channel RVFI contract, or retirement ordering.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the monolithic control propagation with compact execute, memory, writeback, and retirement pipeline record types that retain all required RVFI metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/decoder.sv\",\"description\":\"Keep the strict legal-instruction decode but expose stage-local control fields instead of requiring the full control bundle to cross every stage.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the compact execute micro-op, operands, immediate, register addresses, and precise retirement metadata at the ID/EX boundary.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Consume the execute-local record and emit only the memory/writeback controls, computed result, and retirement metadata needed by later stages.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Use a memory-local record and produce a narrow MEM/WB retirement record, preserving alignment traps, byte masks, load data, and RVFI values.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Reconnect the stage-local records and forwarding/control wiring without changing the top-level IO, single-channel RVFI contract, or retirement ordering.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":400.22,\"delta_pct\":-1.64,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The history rules out broad queues, extra pipeline stages, and predictor-style front-end structures: they either reduced Fmax/IPC or failed RVFI ordering. The strongest remaining structural angle is a narrowly scoped execution sidecar that removes the RV32M arithmetic cones from the ordinary five-stage timing path while keeping common RV32I latency unchanged."}}
