{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r10s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r10s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Decouple RVFI metadata from the execute hot path\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The successful ALU restructuring raised Fmax by removing wide M-extension\n  arithmetic from the ordinary path, but EX/MEM still carries a broad packed\n  record containing retirement-only PC, instruction, source-value, branch, and\n  memory-trace fields. Those fields are not used by forwarding or hazard\n  decisions, yet they cross the same execute boundary and can add routing and\n  fanout to the timing-critical datapath. A same-depth structural split can\n  target this remaining physical overhead without adding instruction latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the EX/MEM and MEM/WB state into a narrow execution sideband and a\n  separate RVFI trace sideband. The hot execution record should contain only\n  the ALU result, store data, destination register, memory controls, and valid\n  state needed by forwarding, hazard control, and the dmem interface. Register\n  the PC, instruction, source addresses and values, resolved next PC, and\n  precise trap/byte-mask metadata in a parallel retirement record that never\n  feeds the EX operand muxes. Recombine the sidebands only at the existing\n  MEM/WB retirement boundary, preserving single-issue RVFI order, load/store\n  semantics, misalignment traps, redirects, and all source-value fields. This\n  should reduce routed fanout on the common execute path while leaving CoreMark\n  IPC and the five-stage latency unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define narrow execute/memory records plus a parallel retirement-trace record, retaining every field required at the existing RVFI boundary.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Register execution results and retirement metadata in separate sidebands, keeping forwarding and redirect logic connected only to the narrow execution record.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the narrow memory record, carry the trace sideband independently, and merge load results, alignment traps, and memory masks at MEM/WB without changing timing.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Reconnect the split pipeline records, forwarding, hazards, writeback, and RVFI outputs while preserving the single-channel retirement contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
