{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The prior structural attempts show three traps: front-end buffering was hurt by redirect/refill bubbles, a memory queue failed liveness/order, and sideband splitting unexpectedly worsened routing. I’m narrowing the proposal to a same-depth structural change that removes common-path fanout without adding speculative state or a new retirement protocol."}}
