d ALU completion skid during data stalls\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"A dmemReady stall currently freezes the entire five-stage machine even when\\\\nthe instruction behind the blocked load or store is an independent integer\\\\noperation. The earlier full elastic-memory queue was too broad and failed\\\\nliveness, while a store-only buffer added arbitration and ordering cost. A\\\\nmuch narrower completion structure can recover some of the lost overlap\\\\nwithout speculating or reordering any memory operation.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"A dmemReady stall currently freezes the entire five-stage machine even when\\\\nthe instruction behind the blocked load or store is an independent integer\\\\noperation. The earlier full elastic-memory queue was too broad and failed\\\\nliveness, while a store-only buffer added arbitration and ordering cost. A\\\\nmuch narrower completion structure can recover some of the lost overlap\\\\nwithout speculating or reordering any memory operation.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry in-order completion skid between EX and MEM that accepts only\\\\nyounger, non-memory, non-control ALU instructions while an older EX/MEM load\\\\nor store waits for io_dmemReady. Keep the blocked memory operation as the\\\\nretirement head, forbid younger loads, stores, branches, jumps, and illegal\\\\noperations from entering the skid, and stop the front end once the skid is\\\\nfull. After the memory completes, drain the skid entry into the normal\\\\nMEM/WB path before accepting another result. Add explicit forwarding from\\\\nthe skid entry and preserve age ordering, precise redirects, RVFI source\\\\nvalues, and register writeback. This limited bypass should hide short random\\\\ndmem stalls with modest area and control overhead while avoiding the timing\\\\nand correctness risks of a general completion queue.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Define a compact completion-skid payload and valid/age metadata for a younger ALU result while retaining the existing RVFI payload fields.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate the one-entry ALU skid between EX and MEM, select the oldest completed result for writeback, and connect skid forwarding without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose a sideband candidate for non-memory, non-control ALU instructions and prevent skid capture of operations that could redirect, trap, or access memory.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add ordered drain/capture behavior so a blocked older data request remains the retirement head and the younger ALU completion reaches MEM/WB only after it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace unconditional dmem-stall freezing with skid-full and dependency-aware backpressure, while keeping memory ordering, load-use hazards, redirect flushes, and forward progress precise.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Give the completion skid highest forwarding priority for dependent ALU operands, with x0 and valid gating and older EX/MEM/MEM/WB priority preserved when the skid is absent.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Define a compact completion-skid payload and valid/age metadata for a younger ALU result while retaining the existing RVFI payload fields.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate the one-entry ALU skid between EX and MEM, select the oldest completed result for writeback, and connect skid forwarding without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose a sideband candidate for non-memory, non-control ALU instructions and prevent skid capture of operations that could redirect, trap, or access memory.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add ordered drain/capture behavior so a blocked older data request remains the retirement head and the younger ALU completion reaches MEM/WB only after it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace unconditional dmem-stall freezing with skid-full and dependency-aware backpressure, while keeping memory ordering, load-use hazards, redirect flushes, and forward progress precise.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Give the completion skid highest forwarding priority for dependent ALU operands, with x0 and valid gating and older EX/MEM/MEM/WB priority preserved when the skid is absent.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 6, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): A one-entry ALU completion skid must separate memory completion, skid capture/drain, and EX/MEM clearing while preserving the single MEM/WB retirement slot and age ordering, or `dmemReady` transitions can corrupt CoreMark execution.\\\"}\\n19:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Tokenized exact-PC loop target predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage core still pays an EX redirect and front-end flush for\\\\nrepeatedly taken CoreMark loops. Earlier BTFNT, RAS, and tagged BTB attempts\\\\nshowed that decoding in IF, carrying a 32-bit prediction through the\\\\npipeline, or adding speculative recovery state can erase the IPC benefit\\\\nand damage Fmax.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage core still pays an EX redirect and front-end flush for\\\\nrepeatedly taken CoreMark loops. Earlier BTFNT, RAS, and tagged BTB attempts\\\\nshowed that decoding in IF, carrying a 32-bit prediction through the\\\\npipeline, or adding speculative recovery state can erase the IPC benefit\\\\nand damage Fmax.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry exact-PC last-target predictor specialized for recurring\\\\ncontrol-transfer PCs. IF uses the registered tag/target hit to fetch the\\\\npredicted target, but carries only a one-bit prediction token with the\\\\ninstruction; EX re-looks up the target and compares it with the resolved\\\\nnext PC. A token is trusted only when the EX lookup still hits and agrees,\\\\nso table replacement, not-taken exits, misaligned targets, and aliases\\\\nalways take the normal precise redirect path. Train only on valid taken\\\\nbranches and jumps, keeping the target mux and pipeline sideband smaller\\\\nthan the prior metadata-heavy BTBs while removing steady-state loop flushes.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a single prediction-token bit to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles without carrying a 32-bit predicted target through the pipeline.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe one-entry exact-PC target table with IF and EX lookup ports and taken-transfer training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the predictor hit target for the next fetch while preserving imem stalls, EX redirect priority, and an atomic per-instruction prediction token.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the prediction token alongside the instruction and decoded control state.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recompute the predicted target from the EX lookup, suppress redirects only for tokenized agreeing predictions, and redirect precisely on misses or exits.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the predictor lookup/training and token-aware redirect path through the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the RVFI contract.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a single prediction-token bit to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles without carrying a 32-bit predicted target through the pipeline.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe one-entry exact-PC target table with IF and EX lookup ports and taken-transfer training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the predictor hit target for the next fetch while preserving imem stalls, EX redirect priority, and an atomic per-instruction prediction token.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the prediction token alongside the instruction and decoded control state.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recompute the predicted target from the EX lookup, suppress redirects only for tokenized agreeing predictions, and redirect precisely on misses or exits.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the predictor lookup/training and token-aware redirect path through the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the RVFI contract.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 401.44, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -1.34, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 41.94, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 173.55, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4323203, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7671, \\\"ff\\\": 1928, \\\"seeds\\\": [173.55, 166.67, 182.48], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T21:58:45.127087Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 6, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (regression, -1.34%): Even a one-entry exact-PC target table with only a one-bit pipeline token can regress CoreMark when IF target selection plus EX re-lookup/agreement and miss-repair redirects cost more than the repeatedly taken loop flushes it removes.\\\"}\\n20:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Consumer-specific EX operand mux factoring\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The optimized core still builds fully forwarded rs1/rs2 operands before\\\\napplying the EX-stage PC/immediate selection. For common ADDI and memory\\\\naddress operations, that leaves an unnecessary forwarding mux on the ALU\\\\ninput even though the instruction cannot use the forwarded value there.\\\\nThe prior ALU optimization improved Fmax without changing IPC, so removing\\\\nanother level of common execute-path muxing is a promising low-risk follow-up.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The optimized core still builds fully forwarded rs1/rs2 operands before\\\\napplying the EX-stage PC/immediate selection. For common ADDI and memory\\\\naddress operations, that leaves an unnecessary forwarding mux on the ALU\\\\ninput even though the instruction cannot use the forwarded value there.\\\\nThe prior ALU optimization improved Fmax without changing IPC, so removing\\\\nanother level of common execute-path muxing is a promising low-risk follow-up.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Factor the EX operand network by consumer: select the immediate directly as\\\\nthe ALU B operand when alu_src is set, and select PC directly as the ALU A\\\\noperand for AUIPC, while retaining the existing freshest-writer forwarding\\\\nmuxes for branch comparisons, stores, JALR, and RVFI source values. This\\\\nshould shorten the dominant address-generation and integer ALU paths and\\\\nreduce forwarding-control fanout without adding latency, changing hazards,\\\\nor changing any architectural result or retirement metadata.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refactor ALU operand selection so immediate and PC consumers bypass irrelevant forwarding mux levels while branches, stores, JALR, and RVFI retain exact forwarded operands.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refactor ALU operand selection so immediate and PC consumers bypass irrelevant forwarding mux levels while branches, stores, JALR, and RVFI retain exact forwarded operands.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 368.01, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -9.55, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 30.12, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 165.29, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7611, \\\"ff\\\": 1875, \\\"seeds\\\": [165.29, 189.43, 162.23], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T22:15:44.680992Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (regression, -9.55%): Consumer-specific EX operand factoring can regress CoreMark when it duplicates the `fwd_rs1_sel`/`fwd_rs2_sel` mux trees for ALU inputs alongside canonical forwarded operands, so shortening nominal immediate/PC paths must be weighed against added mux replication and routing fanout.\\\"}\\n21:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Stage-local micro-op pipeline records\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage datapath currently carries the full control bundle through\\\\nevery pipeline boundary, including branch, memory, execute, and retirement\\\\nfields that are irrelevant to most downstream stages. That creates broad\\\\ncontrol fanout and routing across the EX/MEM and MEM/WB boundaries even\\\\nthough CoreMark is dominated by ordinary ALU and address-generation ops.\\\\nThe prior structural attempts that added queues or pipeline stages paid\\\\nsubstantial control and latency cost; a same-depth restructuring can target\\\\nFmax without adding retirement or dependency latency.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage datapath currently carries the full control bundle through\\\\nevery pipeline boundary, including branch, memory, execute, and retirement\\\\nfields that are irrelevant to most downstream stages. That creates broad\\\\ncontrol fanout and routing across the EX/MEM and MEM/WB boundaries even\\\\nthough CoreMark is dominated by ordinary ALU and address-generation ops.\\\\nThe prior structural attempts that added queues or pipeline stages paid\\\\nsubstantial control and latency cost; a same-depth restructuring can target\\\\nFmax without adding retirement or dependency latency.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Partition the pipeline record into stage-local micro-op controls and a\\\\nseparate retirement metadata payload. Decode still validates the complete\\\\nRV32IM instruction, but ID/EX latches only execute-relevant controls and\\\\noperands; EX/MEM forwards only memory/writeback controls plus the RVFI\\\\nfields needed after execution; and MEM/WB carries only memory-result and\\\\nretirement state. Remove redundant branch-target bookkeeping and unused\\\\ncontrol fields from later records, while preserving valid/flush behavior,\\\\nforwarded source values, precise trap and misalignment metadata, and every\\\\nRVFI field at the existing single retirement boundary. Narrower stage-local\\\\nfanout should improve routed Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the monolithic control propagation with compact execute, memory, writeback, and retirement pipeline record types that retain all required RVFI metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/decoder.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep the strict legal-instruction decode but expose stage-local control fields instead of requiring the full control bundle to cross every stage.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch the compact execute micro-op, operands, immediate, register addresses, and precise retirement metadata at the ID/EX boundary.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the execute-local record and emit only the memory/writeback controls, computed result, and retirement metadata needed by later stages.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use a memory-local record and produce a narrow MEM/WB retirement record, preserving alignment traps, byte masks, load data, and RVFI values.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reconnect the stage-local records and forwarding/control wiring without changing the top-level IO, single-channel RVFI contract, or retirement ordering.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the monolithic control propagation with compact execute, memory, writeback, and retirement pipeline record types that retain all required RVFI metadata.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/decoder.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Keep the strict legal-instruction decode but expose stage-local control fields instead of requiring the full control bundle to cross every stage.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch the compact execute micro-op, operands, immediate, register addresses, and precise retirement metadata at the ID/EX boundary.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the execute-local record and emit only the memory/writeback controls, computed result, and retirement metadata needed by later stages.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use a memory-local record and produce a narrow MEM/WB retirement record, preserving alignment traps, byte masks, load data, and RVFI values.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reconnect the stage-local records and forwarding/control wiring without changing the top-level IO, single-channel RVFI contract, or retirement ordering.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 400.22, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -1.64, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 41.51, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 179.76, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7517, \\\"ff\\\": 1870, \\\"seeds\\\": [176.24, 179.76, 181.52], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T22:17:59.120441Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (regression, -1.64%): Stage-local micro-op typedefs do not guarantee a timing win when EX/MEM still carries broad retirement metadata and the split adds payload repacking and routing, so control partitioning must reduce physical fanout rather than only reorganize fields.\\\"}\\n22:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Aligned JAL early-target predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage core resolves every JAL in EX, so an unconditional call or\\\\njump flushes the sequentially fetched instructions even though its target\\\\nis fully encoded in the instruction and is always taken. Prior BTFNT and\\\\nlearned BTB designs paid broad lookup, target, and recovery overhead across\\\\nthe whole fetch stream; CoreMark should benefit more from a narrowly scoped\\\\npredictor that does not add conditional-history or replacement state.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The five-stage core resolves every JAL in EX, so an unconditional call or\\\\njump flushes the sequentially fetched instructions even though its target\\\\nis fully encoded in the instruction and is always taken. Prior BTFNT and\\\\nlearned BTB designs paid broad lookup, target, and recovery overhead across\\\\nthe whole fetch stream; CoreMark should benefit more from a narrowly scoped\\\\npredictor that does not add conditional-history or replacement state.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a zero-state static predictor that recognizes only aligned RV32I JAL\\\\ninstructions in IF, forms the J-immediate target, and fetches that target on\\\\nthe following cycle. Carry only a one-bit predicted-JAL token with the\\\\ninstruction; EX suppresses its normal JAL redirect only when that token is\\\\npresent and the resolved target is aligned and agrees, while unpredicted or\\\\nmisaligned JALs retain the existing precise redirect/trap path. Restricting\\\\nthe fetch decode to opcode 1101111 avoids branch-history tables, JALR\\\\nspeculation, and a general BTB, aiming to remove call/jump flushes with a\\\\nsmaller Fmax and control penalty than earlier predictor attempts.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a single predicted-JAL token to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles without carrying a target address through the pipeline.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recognize only aligned JAL opcodes, form the J-immediate target, select it for the next fetch, and emit the atomic prediction token while preserving redirect, stall, and reset priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the predicted-JAL token with the instruction and decoded operands so it remains tied to the owning JAL.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compare tokenized JAL prediction against the resolved jump target and suppress only agreeing aligned redirects; preserve precise recovery and misalignment-trap behavior otherwise.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect the prediction token through the existing front-end flush and EX redirect control without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a single predicted-JAL token to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles without carrying a target address through the pipeline.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Recognize only aligned JAL opcodes, form the J-immediate target, select it for the next fetch, and emit the atomic prediction token while preserving redirect, stall, and reset priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the predicted-JAL token with the instruction and decoded operands so it remains tied to the owning JAL.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compare tokenized JAL prediction against the resolved jump target and suppress only agreeing aligned redirects; preserve precise recovery and misalignment-trap behavior otherwise.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect the prediction token through the existing front-end flush and EX redirect control without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 380.51, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -6.48, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 34.54, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 169.03, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4442217, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7613, \\\"ff\\\": 1868, \\\"seeds\\\": [175.47, 169.03, 155.5], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T22:13:35.527172Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r7s2 (regression, -6.48%): Even a zero-state aligned-JAL predictor can regress CoreMark when IF-side J-immediate formation and target addition lengthen the fetch path and the carried prediction token plus EX agreement check add recovery/control overhead that outweighs saved JAL flushes.\\\"}\\n23:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Predecoded class/sub-op ALU control\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current routed critical path starts at an ID/EX ALU-control bit and\\\\ntraverses the execute ALU's 5-bit operation decode before reaching the\\\\nordinary RV32I result and carry-chain logic.  The successful ALU fast-path\\\\nchange removed the large M-extension cone, so reducing control decode and\\\\nmux depth on this remaining common path is a focused next opportunity.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current routed critical path starts at an ID/EX ALU-control bit and\\\\ntraverses the execute ALU's 5-bit operation decode before reaching the\\\\nordinary RV32I result and carry-chain logic.  The successful ALU fast-path\\\\nchange removed the large M-extension cone, so reducing control decode and\\\\nmux depth on this remaining common path is a focused next opportunity.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Predecode the ALU control in ID into an explicit M-extension class bit and\\\\ncompact RV32I/M sub-operation fields, then pipeline those fields instead of\\\\nmaking EX rediscover operation classes with range comparisons and a broad\\\\n5-bit case select.  Implement the RV32I fast path with direct class/sub-op\\\\nselects and keep the existing isolated multiply/divide path behind the M\\\\nbit.  Preserve every RV32I and RV32M result, RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior,\\\\nillegal-instruction handling, forwarding, and the unchanged single-cycle\\\\nexecute/retirement schedule.  The expected gain is lower control-to-ALU\\\\ndelay and reduced control fanout with no IPC cost.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact predecoded ALU class/sub-operation fields to the pipeline control bundle while retaining all existing trap and memory controls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/decoder.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generate the explicit M-class and compact ALU sub-operation controls only inside validated RV32IM opcode/funct matches, preserving strict illegal defaults.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch the predecoded ALU class/sub-operation controls into ID/EX without changing operand, hazard, or RVFI metadata timing.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the predecoded class/sub-operation selects to bypass 5-bit range/equality decoding on the common RV32I path while preserving real M arithmetic and ALTOPS semantics.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact predecoded ALU class/sub-operation fields to the pipeline control bundle while retaining all existing trap and memory controls.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/decoder.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generate the explicit M-class and compact ALU sub-operation controls only inside validated RV32IM opcode/funct matches, preserving strict illegal defaults.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Latch the predecoded ALU class/sub-operation controls into ID/EX without changing operand, hazard, or RVFI metadata timing.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the predecoded class/sub-operation selects to bypass 5-bit range/equality decoding on the common RV32I path while preserving real M arithmetic and ALTOPS semantics.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 318.29, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -21.77, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 12.54, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 142.96, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7468, \\\"ff\\\": 1869, \\\"seeds\\\": [142.96, 141.94, 164.04], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T22:35:22.761062Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 8, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r8s0 (regression, -21.77%): Predecoding ALU class/sub-operation fields did not pay off when the added ID/EX control fields and fanout outweighed removing EX range comparisons, showing that narrower control encoding helps only if it also reduces physical routing on the common CoreMark path.\\\"}\\n25:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Retirement-trained loop target cache\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Prior predictors either put branch decode and target arithmetic on the IF\\\\ncritical path or carried broad prediction state through every pipeline\\\\nstage. The exact-PC target attempt was close to neutral, suggesting that\\\\nthe useful signal is recurring taken loops, but the predictor must be\\\\nnarrower and must not be polluted by calls, returns, or speculative\\\\nwrong-path training.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Prior predictors either put branch decode and target arithmetic on the IF\\\\ncritical path or carried broad prediction state through every pipeline\\\\nstage. The exact-PC target attempt was close to neutral, suggesting that\\\\nthe useful signal is recurring taken loops, but the predictor must be\\\\nnarrower and must not be polluted by calls, returns, or speculative\\\\nwrong-path training.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a tiny direct-mapped loop-target cache trained only when a backward\\\\nconditional branch retires. Each entry stores an exact PC tag, its resolved\\\\ntarget, and an armed bit; IF uses a registered tag/target hit to redirect\\\\nonly recurring loop branches. Carry only a compact cache-slot token with\\\\nthe instruction, and protect the matching entry until EX resolves it so\\\\ntable replacement cannot make an old prediction appear correct. A taken\\\\nhit suppresses the normal EX redirect, while a loop exit invalidates the\\\\nentry and follows the existing precise redirect path. Training at\\\\nretirement prevents wrong-path branches from changing predictor state and\\\\nthe loop-only scope avoids adding JAL/JALR traffic to the hot predictor.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact loop-prediction token and validity fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles without carrying a 32-bit predicted target.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a small exact-PC loop-target cache with retirement training, armed/invalidation state, IF lookup, EX agreement lookup, and protection for an in-flight prediction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use only a loop-cache hit to select the next fetch PC, preserving imem stalls, redirect priority, and atomic prediction-token generation.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the compact loop-cache token with the owning instruction and preserve flush/stall behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Suppress redirects only for an armed loop-cache token whose resolved taken target agrees; retain precise recovery and misalignment traps for exits and misses.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect IF/EX predictor lookups and retirement-only training while keeping the single-issue RVFI contract and monotonic retirement unchanged.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact loop-prediction token and validity fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles without carrying a 32-bit predicted target.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a small exact-PC loop-target cache with retirement training, armed/invalidation state, IF lookup, EX agreement lookup, and protection for an in-flight prediction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use only a loop-cache hit to select the next fetch PC, preserving imem stalls, redirect priority, and atomic prediction-token generation.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the compact loop-cache token with the owning instruction and preserve flush/stall behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Suppress redirects only for an armed loop-cache token whose resolved taken target agrees; retain precise recovery and misalignment traps for exits and misses.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect IF/EX predictor lookups and retirement-only training while keeping the single-issue RVFI contract an