elect the ALU subtract operation and expose the\\n  subtract result flags (zero, unsigned borrow, and overflow-corrected signed\\n  less-than) from the ALU. Replace the separate EX branch-difference logic\\n  with those flags, allowing the ALU's existing fast-path subtract carry\\n  chain to serve both its result and all branch predicates. Keep branch\\n  target arithmetic, forwarding, misalignment traps, RVFI metadata, and\\n  RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS behavior unchanged. This preserves IPC and may reduce\\n  duplicated arithmetic/routing on the branch redirect path.\\nexpected_impact:\\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\\n  confidence: low\\nchanges:\\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\\n    description: \\\"Expose shared subtract zero, borrow, and signed-less-than flags alongside the existing RV32I fast-path result, preserving real and ALTOPS M-extension behavior.\\\"\\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\\n    description: \\\"Set the validated conditional-branch control to use the ALU subtract operation without changing branch legality or operands.\\\"\\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n    description: \\\"Consume ALU-provided compare flags for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU and remove the duplicate EX branch subtract cone while retaining redirect and trap semantics.\\\"\\n\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r11s0\\\"\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n16:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Wrote the hypothesis:\\n\\n[ hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml ](/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep3/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml)\\n\\nIt targets ALU subtract-flag reuse for branch comparisons, preserving the RVFI and pipeline contract.\"}}\n17-{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":306472,\"cached_input_tokens\":215552,\"output_tokens\":3656,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":2383}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining high-upside structural opportunity is the memory hierarchy: the current core sends every normal load/store through the stalled external dmem port, while CoreMark repeatedly touches a small working set. I’m proposing a bounded, direct-mapped write-through data cache with explicit MMIO bypass and a single in-order miss/refill path, keeping retirement and memory ordering unchanged."}}
