thmetic cones on\\nthe common EX path materially limit Tang Nano 20K Fmax.  The current EX\\nstage independently computes pc+imm for branches and JAL and rs1+imm for\\nJALR, even though only one control-flow target is needed for an instruction.\\nThose parallel adders and the following mux add fanout to the same stage\\nwithout improving ordinary integer throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The successful ALU optimization showed that redundant arithmetic cones on\\nthe common EX path materially limit Tang Nano 20K Fmax.  The current EX\\nstage independently computes pc+imm for branches and JAL and rs1+imm for\\nJALR, even though only one control-flow target is needed for an instruction.\\nThose parallel adders and the following mux add fanout to the same stage\\nwithout improving ordinary integer throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the separate branch-target adder and JALR adder with one\\ncontrol-gated target adder whose base is selected between PC and forwarded\\nrs1.  Reuse its result for both branch and jump target formation, retaining\\nJALR bit-zero clearing, misaligned-target trapping, redirect priority, and\\nthe existing RVFI pc_next behavior.  This should reduce EX arithmetic area\\nand control-to-target mux depth while leaving the retirement schedule and\\nCoreMark IPC unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Fuse branch, JAL, and JALR target formation into one gated PC/rs1 plus immediate adder while preserving redirect and misalignment-trap semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Fuse branch, JAL, and JALR target formation into one gated PC/rs1 plus immediate adder while preserving redirect and misalignment-trap semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 372.99, \"delta_pct\": -8.33, \"vs_baseline\": 31.88, \"fmax_mhz\": 167.53, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7520, \"ff\": 1868, \"seeds\": [142.15, 171.64, 167.53], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T20:47:42.421311Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -8.33%): Sharing branch/JAL/JALR target arithmetic through a control-gated `target_base` mux and common `target_sum` can worsen CoreMark when the added EX selection and fanout cost more than the removed parallel adders, so arithmetic sharing must be evaluated against its control-path depth.\"}\n9:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"ID-stage early control-transfer resolution\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently resolves conditional branches and jumps\\nin EX, flushing younger work and paying a multi-cycle redirect penalty on\\nCoreMark's tight loops. The earlier fetch-prediction experiments added\\ntiming and recovery cost on the IF path, so the useful structural opportunity\\nis to shorten the control hazard without decoding branches during fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently resolves conditional branches and jumps\\nin EX, flushing younger work and paying a multi-cycle redirect penalty on\\nCoreMark's tight loops. The earlier fetch-prediction experiments added\\ntiming and recovery cost on the IF path, so the useful structural opportunity\\nis to shorten the control hazard without decoding branches during fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move legal conditional-branch and jump target/condition resolution into ID\\nwith a dedicated PC-plus-immediate adder and comparator. Add decode-stage\\noperand bypasses from EX/MEM and MEM/WB, and conservatively stall only when\\na branch operand is still waiting on a load or an unresolved producer. Use\\nthe early redirect to flush just the younger fetch work, while carrying the\\nresolved next-PC and misalignment-trap metadata into retirement so RVFI,\\nordering, and illegal-instruction behavior remain unchanged. Removing the\\nbranch comparator/target path from EX should reduce taken-loop bubbles\\nwithout putting instruction decode or target formation on the IF critical\\npath.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with resolved next-PC and control-transfer fault metadata needed for precise RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment traps.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve legal branches, JAL, and JALR in ID using dedicated target/compare logic and explicit operand bypass inputs, while exporting an early redirect and trap decision.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Prioritize the ID-stage redirect over sequential fetch, coordinate one-cycle flushes with the existing EX and dmem-stall controls, and wire resolved next-PC data to retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage dependency checks so branches and JALR wait for unavailable load results while allowing EX/MEM and MEM/WB ALU results to bypass into ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the ID-resolved transfer metadata, retain a precise fallback for malformed or misaligned transfers, and remove redundant EX control-transfer work from the timing-critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with resolved next-PC and control-transfer fault metadata needed for precise RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment traps.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve legal branches, JAL, and JALR in ID using dedicated target/compare logic and explicit operand bypass inputs, while exporting an early redirect and trap decision.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Prioritize the ID-stage redirect over sequential fetch, coordinate one-cycle flushes with the existing EX and dmem-stall controls, and wire resolved next-PC data to retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage dependency checks so branches and JALR wait for unavailable load results while allowing EX/MEM and MEM/WB ALU results to bypass into ID.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the ID-resolved transfer metadata, retain a precise fallback for malformed or misaligned transfers, and remove redundant EX control-transfer work from the timing-critical path.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\neturncode=0)\\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:02 (2)\\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:30  Status: passed\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:31 (31)\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:23 (23)\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: pc_fwd_ch0\\n\\n--- pc_fwd_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\