prior general completion-queue attempt failed\\\\nliveness, so a bounded store-only structure is a lower-risk way to overlap\\\\nthe benchmark's random data-bus stalls without introducing broad out-of-order\\\\nretirement machinery.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry FIFO store buffer at the MEM boundary. A store is accepted\\\\ninto the buffer and retires in program order, while the buffer independently\\\\nholds its address, byte mask, and replicated write data until io_dmemReady\\\\nacknowledges the write. Allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed\\\\nbehind a buffered store; keep younger loads ordered by stalling them on a\\\\npossible store-buffer address conflict, and stop the front end only when the\\\\nbuffer is full or an older memory-order condition requires it. Keep loads,\\\\nRVFI fields, redirects, and trap handling on the existing precise path so\\\\nthis structural change primarily removes store-induced global bubbles.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 374.56, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -7.94, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 32.44, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 166.97, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4457730, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7622, \\\"ff\\\": 1870, \\\"seeds\\\": [172.47, 166.97, 160.49], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T21:18:00.493070Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 4, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -7.94%): On a single-ported dmem, a one-entry store buffer can lose to its own store-priority arbitration, address-conflict checks, and MEM-stage load-forward path, whose control and conservative ordering stalls outweigh the store bubbles they hide in CoreMark.\\\"}\\n13:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Tiny fully tagged last-target predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Taken-loop redirects are still paid in EX, but the earlier BTFNT and RAS\\\\nexperiments showed that fetch-time instruction decoding and speculative\\\\nstack bookkeeping can cost more timing and area than they save. A single\\\\nfully tagged entry can learn the hot target of the most recently taken\\\\ncontrol-transfer PC with substantially less state and no dependence on\\\\nimemData in the fetch critical path.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Taken-loop redirects are still paid in EX, but the earlier BTFNT and RAS\\\\nexperiments showed that fetch-time instruction decoding and speculative\\\\nstack bookkeeping can cost more timing and area than they save. A single\\\\nfully tagged entry can learn the hot target of the most recently taken\\\\ncontrol-transfer PC with substantially less state and no dependence on\\\\nimemData in the fetch critical path.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry last-target branch buffer indexed by an exact full-PC tag.\\\\nOn a hit, fetch advances directly to the recorded target while the\\\\ncurrent instruction carries prediction-valid and predicted-next-PC bits\\\\nthrough ID/EX. Train the entry only from a valid EX-resolved taken branch,\\\\nJAL, or JALR; invalidate it when a matching conditional branch resolves\\\\nnot-taken. EX compares the carried prediction with the resolved next PC,\\\\nsuppressing the normal redirect on a hit and redirecting plus flushing on\\\\nevery miss. This preserves precise RVFI pc_wdata and recovery while\\\\navoiding fetch-time opcode/immediate decode and limiting predictor muxing\\\\nto one tag compare and target mux.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement the one-entry fully tagged last-target buffer, including exact-PC lookup, taken-transfer training, matching not-taken invalidation, and reset state.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Give fetch a predicted target input with imemReady and EX-redirect priority, advancing on a valid predictor hit without flushing the currently fetched instruction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the decoded instruction without altering decoder legality or register operands.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compare predicted next PC against the resolved branch/jump next PC, generate redirects only for misses or unpredicted transfers, and retain precise misalignment-trap behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate and wire the predictor lookup/training path, coordinate predictor-hit and EX-mispredict control with existing flushes, and preserve RVFI retirement ordering.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement the one-entry fully tagged last-target buffer, including exact-PC lookup, taken-transfer training, matching not-taken invalidation, and reset state.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Give fetch a predicted target input with imemReady and EX-redirect priority, advancing on a valid predictor hit without flushing the currently fetched instruction.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the decoded instruction without altering decoder legality or register operands.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compare predicted next PC against the resolved branch/jump next PC, generate redirects only for misses or unpredicted transfers, and retain precise misalignment-trap behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate and wire the predictor lookup/training path, coordinate predictor-hit and EX-mispredict control with existing flushes, and preserve RVFI retirement ordering.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\\\n:SS (secs)]: 0:00:10 (10)\\\\nSBY 18:07:59 [cover] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\\\nSBY 18:07:59 [cover] summary: cover trace: cover/engine_0/trace0.vcd\\\\nSBY 18:07:59 [cover] summary:   reached cover statement rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__cover_cover_stmts_vh_1_48 at cover_stmts.vh:1.23-1.55 step 20\\\\nSBY 18:07:59 [cover] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\\\nSBY 18:08:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:01  waiting for solver (1 minute)\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:11  Status: passed\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:11 (71)\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:59 (59)\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\\\nSBY 18:08:49 [reg_ch0] DONE