r completion, or all four M-operation checks and `reg_ch0` can fail together.\\\"}\\n28:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r9s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Epoch-qualified one-entry loop predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loops, but prior BTBs and\\\\nstatic predictors paid too much IF timing and pipeline metadata overhead.\\\\nThe one-entry exact-PC target experiment was close to neutral, making a\\\\nsmaller loop-only predictor with stronger prediction/repair atomicity the\\\\nmost promising remaining predictor direction.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark repeatedly executes backward conditional loops, but prior BTBs and\\\\nstatic predictors paid too much IF timing and pipeline metadata overhead.\\\\nThe one-entry exact-PC target experiment was close to neutral, making a\\\\nsmaller loop-only predictor with stronger prediction/repair atomicity the\\\\nmost promising remaining predictor direction.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a one-entry exact-PC loop-target predictor that is trained only by a\\\\nretiring, taken backward conditional branch and is enabled only after the\\\\ntarget has been observed. IF performs just a tag compare and target mux,\\\\nwith no opcode or immediate decode; the instruction carries a compact\\\\nprediction token plus predictor epoch, while EX revalidates the same entry\\\\nand suppresses its redirect only for an epoch-matched taken target. A\\\\npredicted loop exit redirects to the fall-through path and invalidates the\\\\nentry at retirement. Epoch-qualified lookup and retirement-only training\\\\nkeep replacement, stalls, flushes, RVFI pc_wdata, and wrong-path state from\\\\ncreating the pc_fwd failure seen in the earlier loop-target cache.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact loop-prediction valid/epoch fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX records without carrying a predicted 32-bit target through the pipeline.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement the one-entry exact-PC backward-loop target state, IF tag/target lookup, epoch tracking, EX revalidation, and retirement-only taken/exit training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use an epoch-qualified predictor hit to select the next fetch PC while preserving imemReady, redirect, reset, and flush priority and emitting an atomic prediction token.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the prediction token and captured epoch with its owning instruction, clearing them on bubbles and redirects.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compare the prediction token and epoch-qualified predictor hit with the resolved branch next PC, suppressing only an agreeing taken-loop redirect and repairing all mismatches precisely.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect predictor lookup, EX validation, and MEM/WB retirement training without changing the single-channel RVFI contract or retirement ordering.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact loop-prediction valid/epoch fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX records without carrying a predicted 32-bit target through the pipeline.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement the one-entry exact-PC backward-loop target state, IF tag/target lookup, epoch tracking, EX revalidation, and retirement-only taken/exit training.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use an epoch-qualified predictor hit to select the next fetch PC while preserving 