cone may\\\\nimprove Fmax without adding pipeline latency or changing IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"EX currently expresses BEQ, BNE, signed, and unsigned relational branches\\\\nas separate high-level comparisons selected by a branch-op case. That can\\\\nreplicate comparator logic on the redirect path even though all predicates\\\\nare functions of the same rs1-rs2 subtraction. CoreMark contains frequent\\\\nloop and conditional branches, so shortening this control-flow cone may\\\\nimprove Fmax without adding pipeline latency or changing IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the EX branch comparison case with one 33-bit unsigned subtraction\\\\nthat supplies zero, borrow, and signed-less-than flags. Select BEQ/BNE from\\\\nthe zero flag and BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU from the corresponding signed or unsigned\\\\nflag. Preserve the existing branch target adder, redirect priority,\\\\nmisalignment trap handling, forwarding, and RVFI metadata. Sharing the\\\\ncomparison flags should reduce duplicated relational/equality cones and\\\\nfanout on the branch redirect path while leaving all non-branch execution\\\\nbehavior unchanged.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Derive all RV32I branch predicates from a shared 33-bit rs1-rs2 subtract flag network while preserving exact signed/unsigned semantics and existing redirect/trap behavior.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Derive all RV32I branch predicates from a shared 33-bit rs1-rs2 subtract flag network while preserving exact signed/unsigned semantics and existing redirect/trap behavior.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"improvement\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 412.38, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 1.35, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 45.81, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 185.22, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7500, \\\"ff\\\": 1862, \\\"seeds\\\": [187.48, 185.22, 174.67], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T23:03:41.188190Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 10, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r10s0 (improvement, +1.35%): A single 33-bit EX subtract with zero, borrow, and overflow-corrected signed-less-than flags can modestly improve CoreMark by sharing BEQ/BNE and signed/unsigned relational branch cones without adding pipeline latency.\\\"}\\n30:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Decouple RVFI metadata from the execute hot path\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The successful ALU restructuring raised Fmax by removing wide M-extension\\\\narithmetic from the ordinary path, but EX/MEM still carries a broad packed\\\\nrecord containing retirement-only PC, instruction, source-value, branch, and\\\\nmemory-trace fields. Those fields are not used by forwarding or hazard\\\\ndecisions, yet they cross the same execute boundary and can add routing and\\\\nfanout to the timing-critical datapath. A same-depth structural split can\\\\ntarget this remaining physical overhead without adding instruction latency.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The successful ALU restructuring raised Fmax by removing wide M-extension\\\\narithmetic from the ordinary path, but EX/MEM still carries a broad packed\\\\nrecord containing retirement-only PC, instruction, source-value, branch, and\\\\nmemory-trace fields. Those fields are not used by forwarding or hazard\\\\ndecisions, yet they cross the same execute boundary and can add routing and\\\\nfanout to the timing-critical datapath. A same-depth structural split can\\\\ntarget this remaining physical overhead without adding instruction latency.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Split the EX/MEM and MEM/WB state into a narrow execution sideband and a\\\\nseparate RVFI trace sideband. The hot execution record should contain only\\\\nthe ALU result, store data, destination register, memory controls, and valid\\\\nstate needed by forwarding, hazard control, and the dmem interface. Register\\\\nthe PC, instruction, source addresses and values, resolved next PC, and\\\\nprecise trap/byte-mask metadata in a parallel retirement record that never\\\\nfeeds the EX operand muxes. Recombine the sidebands only at the existing\\\\nMEM/WB retirement boundary, preserving single-issue RVFI order, load/store\\\\nsemantics, misalignment traps, redirects, and all source-value fields. This\\\\nshould reduce routed fanout on the common execute path while leaving CoreMark\\\\nIPC and the five-stage latency unchanged.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Define narrow execute/memory records plus a parallel retirement-trace record, retaining every field required at the existing RVFI boundary.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Register execution results and retirement metadata in separate sidebands, keeping forwarding and redirect logic connected only to the narrow execution record.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the narrow memory record, carry the trace sideband independently, and merge load results, alignment traps, and memory masks at MEM/WB without changing timing.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reconnect the split pipeline records, forwarding, hazards, writeback, and RVFI outputs while preserving the single-channel retirement contract.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Define narrow execute/memory records plus a parallel retirement-trace record, retaining every field required at the existing RVFI boundary.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Register execution results and retirement metadata in separate sidebands, keeping forwarding and redirect logic connected only to the narrow execution record.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the narrow memory record, carry the trace sideband independently, and merge load results, alignment traps, and memory masks at MEM/WB without changing timing.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Reconnect the split pipeline records, forwarding, hazards, writeback, and RVFI outputs while preserving the single-channel retirement contract.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 386.0, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -5.13, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 36.48, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 173.37, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4491485, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7764, \\\"ff\\\": 1868, \\\"seeds\\\": [171.94, 173.37, 176.43], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T23:15:48.921278Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 10}\\n31:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r10s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Atomic target-token loop predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark still pays the EX redirect and wrong-path flush for recurring\\\\ntaken loops. The prior exact-PC predictor was nearly neutral because its\\\\nIF target mux was combined with an EX table re-lookup and miss repair, and\\\\nthe epoch-qualified variants failed pc_fwd when predictor state changed\\\\nbetween fetch and resolution.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"CoreMark still pays the EX redirect and wrong-path flush for recurring\\\\ntaken loops. The prior exact-PC predictor was nearly neutral because its\\\\nIF target mux was combined with an EX table re-lookup and miss repair, and\\\\nthe epoch-qualified variants failed pc_fwd when predictor state changed\\\\nbetween fetch and resolution.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a tiny one-entry last-target predictor trained only by retiring taken\\\\nbackward conditional branches. On an IF hit, capture the predicted target\\\\natomically with the instruction and use it for the next PC; carry that\\\\nexact target with the instruction rather than re-reading mutable predictor\\\\nstate in EX. EX suppresses the redirect only when the captured target,\\\\nresolved taken target, and alignment all agree. Any loop exit, alias, table\\\\nreplacement, or stale prediction therefore follows the normal redirect\\\\npath, while eliminating the EX re-lookup and epoch-sensitive acceptance\\\\nlogic from the prior attempts.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add an atomic prediction-valid bit and captured predicted-next-PC field to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, with zeroed bubble values.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe one-entry exact-PC backward-loop target predictor with retirement-only training and a combinational IF lookup.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the predictor hit to select the next fetch PC and capture the exact target alongside the fetched instruction, preserving redirect, stall, and reset priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the immutable prediction token and captured target with the owning instruction, clearing both on flushes and bubbles.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Validate predictions solely from the captured target and current resolved branch result, suppressing only an exact aligned taken match and repairing all mismatches precisely.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect predictor lookup and retirement training while keeping RVFI pc_wdata, retirement order, and single-channel behavior unchanged.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add an atomic prediction-valid bit and captured predicted-next-PC field to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, with zeroed bubble values.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe one-entry exact-PC backward-loop target predictor with retirement-only training and a combinational IF lookup.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the predictor hit to select the next fetch PC and capture the exact target alongside the fetched instruction, preserving redirect, stall, and reset priority.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the immutable prediction token and captured target with the owning instruction, clearing both on flushes and bubbles.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Validate predictions solely from the captured target and current resolved branch result, suppressing only an exact aligned taken match and repairing all mismatches precisely.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect predictor lookup and retirement training while keeping RVFI pc_wdata, retirement order, and single-channel behavior unchanged.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 247.09, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -39.27, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -12.63, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 106.54, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4311793, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 7831, \\\"ff\\\": 1976, \\\"seeds\\\": [106.54, 118.11, 103.89], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T23:06:20.937734Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 10, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r10s2 (regression, -39.27%): Making a one-entry loop target immutable with the instruction does not make prediction profitable when every hit still drives an IF next-PC mux and IF/ID/EX token path, while alias or stale hits require EX repair redirects that outweigh saved CoreMark loop flushes.\\\"}\\n33:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r11s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Small direct-mapped write-through data cache\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Every normal load and store currently reaches the external dmem port, so\\\\nthe benchmark's random dmemReady stalls freeze the entire in-order pipe.\\\\nCoreMark repeatedly accesses a small working set, and the FPGA has block\\\\nRAM resources that can hold a modest cache without adding a new pipeline\\\\nstage or speculative control state.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Every normal load and store currently reaches the external dmem port, so\\\\nthe benchmark's random dmemReady stalls freeze the entire in-order pipe.\\\\nCoreMark repeatedly accesses a small working set, and the FPGA has block\\\\nRAM resources that can hold a modest cache without adding a new pipeline\\\\nstage or speculative control state.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a 2 KiB direct-mapped write-through data cache with four-word lines for\\\\nthe normal RAM range only. A load hit returns the cached word locally and\\\\navoids the external dmem handshake; a miss holds the oldest request and\\\\nrefills the line in order before releasing the pipeline. Stores remain\\\\nwrite-through, update a valid cache line on a hit, and use no-write-allocate\\\\non a miss. Explicitly bypass the cache for UART/marker MMIO and perform\\\\nalignment checks before lookup, while preserving the existing MEM/WB and\\\\nRVFI memory fields. Repeated CoreMark accesses should therefore avoid many\\\\nrandom dmem stalls while retirement remains single-issue and in order.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/data_cache.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe direct-mapped four-word-line write-through cache for normal RAM, with tag/valid storage, hit response, serialized miss refill, store masks, and explicit MMIO bypass.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Place the cache between EX/MEM and the existing dmem/MEM-WB boundary, holding one oldest request through refill or write-through completion while preserving alignment traps, byte lanes, load extension, and RVFI raw-memory reporting.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the cache request/response and busy signals into the existing hazard and dmem-stall control so cache hits flow at one per cycle and misses cannot duplicate, reorder, or double-retire an instruction.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/data_cache.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe direct-mapped four-word-line write-through cache for normal RAM, with tag/valid storage, hit response, serialized miss refill, store masks, and explicit MMIO bypass.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Place the cache between EX/MEM and the existing dmem/MEM-WB boundary, holding one oldest request through refill or write-through completion while preserving alignment traps, byte lanes, load extension, and RVFI raw-memory reporting.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the cache request/response and busy signals into the existing hazard and dmem-stall control so cache hits flow at one per cycle and misses cannot duplicate, reorder, or double-retire an instruction.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 11, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r11s1 (broken, n/a): A cache integration that instantiates `data_cache` without adding its module to the `rtl/*.sv` build inputs is structurally incomplete and fails cosim before cache performance can be measured.\\\"}\\n34:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r11s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Committed return-only stack predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The previous BTFNT, BTB, and loop-target predictors paid more IF timing,\\\\nmetadata routing, and recovery cost than their saved conditional-branch\\\\nredirects were worth. CoreMark still has frequent call/return control flow,\\\\nso a narrowly scoped indirect-return predictor is a better area/timing\\\\ntradeoff than another general target table.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The previous BTFNT, BTB, and loop-target predictors paid more IF timing,\\\\nmetadata routing, and recovery cost than their saved conditional-branch\\\\nredirects were worth. CoreMark still has frequent call/return control flow,\\\\nso a narrowly scoped indirect-return predictor is a better area/timing\\\\ntradeoff than another general target table.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a two-entry committed return-address stack that predicts only canonical\\\\nJALR returns using x1/x5, with calls pushing pc+4 and returns popping only at\\\\nretirement. Keep predictor state non-speculative: no checkpoints, epochs, or\\\\nupdates from flushed instructions. Carry only a compact return prediction\\\\ntoken and validate the captured target against the resolved JALR target and\\\\nthe owning instruction PC; any miss, alias, non-return JALR, stall, or\\\\nmisaligned target takes the existing precise redirect/recovery path. This\\\\nshould remove recurring return flushes while limiting IF lookup and control\\\\nfanout to indirect-return sites instead of burdening every branch.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe two-entry committed return-address stack, canonical call/return classification, IF lookup, and retirement-only push/pop updates.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact return-prediction-valid, target, and owning-PC token fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, with deterministic bubble values.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the return-only lookup to select a predicted fetch target while preserving imemReady, reset, redirect priority, and sequential fallback.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the immutable return prediction token with its instruction and clear it on bubbles or flushes.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Validate a return prediction against the resolved JALR target and instruction PC, suppressing redirects only for exact aligned matches and repairing all misses.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect prediction lookup, EX validation, and retirement push/pop training without changing the single-channel RVFI contract or order.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Implement a reset-safe two-entry committed return-address stack, canonical call/return classification, IF lookup, and retirement-only push/pop updates.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact return-prediction-valid, target, and owning-PC token fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, with deterministic bubble values.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use the return-only lookup to select a predicted fetch target while preserving imemReady, reset, redirect priority, and sequential fallback.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Pipeline the immutable return prediction token with its instruction and clear it on bubbles or flushes.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Validate a return prediction against the resolved JALR target and instruction PC, suppressing redirects only for exact aligned matches and repairing all misses.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Connect prediction lookup, EX validation, and retirement push/pop training without changing the single-channel RVFI contract or order.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\\\ne=0)\\\\nSBY 20:27:53 [insn_xori_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\\\nSBY 20:27:53 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\\\nSBY 20:27:53 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\\\nSBY 20:27:53 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\\\nSBY 20:27:53 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\\\nSBY 20:27:53 [insn_xori_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\\\nSBY 20:28:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:46  Status: passed\\\\nSBY 20:28:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\\\nSBY 20:28:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\\\nSBY 20:28:27 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:M