{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r12s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Integrated direct-mapped data cache\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current MEM stage sends every ordinary load and store to the external\n  data bus, and a low io_dmemReady freezes the whole five-stage pipeline.\n  CoreMark's 6 KB working set has substantial temporal locality, so a small\n  persistent cache can remove repeated random dmem stalls without adding a\n  speculative front end or changing retirement width.\nhypothesis: |\n  Integrate a reset-safe 2 KiB direct-mapped, four-word-line, write-through\n  data cache directly into the MEM boundary. Cache only aligned accesses in\n  the normal RAM window; bypass UART and marker MMIO, and turn misaligned\n  accesses into the existing precise traps before lookup. A load hit should\n  complete locally and avoid io_dmemReady, while a miss should hold the\n  oldest request and refill its line through a small explicit miss FSM.\n  Stores should update a hit line and remain externally write-through, with\n  no-write-allocate on a miss. Export a cache-busy/request-active condition\n  to hazard control so only real misses or outstanding writes stall, while\n  RVFI reports only the architectural access and preserves in-order single\n  retirement, byte masks, and load sign extension.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the direct-mapped tag, valid, and line-data arrays plus a serialized ready-aware refill/write-through FSM, with normal-RAM lookup, MMIO bypass, alignment handling, and unchanged RVFI memory reporting.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the integrated cache's effective memory request, response data, and busy state to the existing MEM/WB, writeback, forwarding, and retirement paths without changing the top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use cache hit/busy status rather than raw dmemReady to freeze the pipeline, retaining precise ordering and ensuring a miss or write-through transaction cannot duplicate or bypass the EX/MEM request.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
