{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]).keys' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Placement-bounded tiny data cache\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current blocking MEM boundary sends every normal-RAM access through the\n  externally stalled dmem port. The previous 2 KiB cache direction was\n  placement_failed, so the next structural attempt should preserve locality\n  benefits while using a deliberately small state and control footprint.\nhypothesis: |\n  Integrate a 256-byte direct-mapped, four-word-line write-through cache in\n  the MEM boundary, with only sixteen lines of tag/valid/data state. Aligned\n  normal-RAM loads should return on a hit without consulting io_dmemReady;\n  misses should hold the oldest request and refill one line in order, while\n  stores update a hit line and remain write-through with no-write-allocate on\n  a miss. Bypass UART and marker MMIO, perform alignment traps before lookup,\n  and keep the existing single MEM/WB retirement and RVFI reporting. The\n  reduced array and narrow miss FSM should fit the FPGA placement budget while\n  removing repeated CoreMark working-set accesses from the random dmem-stall\n  path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a 16-line, four-word-line write-through cache directly at the MEM boundary, including reset-safe valid/tag/data state, hit handling, serialized refill, MMIO bypass, byte masks, alignment traps, and unchanged RVFI metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire cache hit, miss, and transaction-busy status through the existing MEM/WB and forwarding paths without changing the top-level IO or single-retirement contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace raw dmemReady gating with cache transaction busy/complete gating so hits proceed without a pipeline stall while misses and write-through operations hold the in-flight memory instruction exactly once.\"\n[\"id\", \"title\", \"category\", \"motivation\", \"hypothesis\", \"expected_impact\", \"changes\"]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
