{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"structural\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.delta_pct // \\\"n/a\\\"),(.fitness // \\\"n/a\\\"),(.lesson // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\tDecoupled instruction prefetch FIFO\tregression\t7.15\t303.05\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r1s1 (regression, +7.15%): A small prefetch FIFO is not automatically beneficial when EX redirects flush every queued instruction and FIFO-empty refill inserts ID bubbles, so redirect frequency and refill cost can outweigh hiding random imem backpressure in CoreMark.\nhyp-20260710-002-r2s1\tElastic in-order data-memory completion queue\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t\nhyp-20260710-002-r3s1\tID-stage early control-transfer resolution\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): ID-stage branch and jump redirects must latch resolved next-PC and misalignment-trap metadata with the instruction through ID/EX to retirement, because advancing fetch without keeping RVFI `pc_wdata` aligned can fail `pc_fwd` even when instruction checks pass.\nhyp-20260710-002-r4s1\tSingle-entry nonblocking store buffer\tregression\t-7.94\t374.56\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -7.94%): On a single-ported dmem, a one-entry store buffer can lose to its own store-priority arbitration, address-conflict checks, and MEM-stage load-forward path, whose control and conservative ordering stalls outweigh the store bubbles they hide in CoreMark.\nhyp-20260710-002-r5s1\tRetimed two-stage execute pipeline\tregression\t-53.64\t188.61\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -53.64%): Retiming EX into EX1/EX2 made dependency, redirect, and dmem-stall interlocks pay extra latency on common in-order paths, so CoreMark IPC loss overwhelmed any Fmax benefit; deeper pipelines need latency-aware bypassing without serializing ALU chains.\nhyp-20260710-002-r6s1\tConstrained ALU completion skid during data stalls\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): A one-entry ALU completion skid must separate memory completion, skid capture/drain, and EX/MEM clearing while preserving the single MEM/WB retirement slot and age ordering, or `dmemReady` transitions can corrupt CoreMark execution.\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tStage-local micro-op pipeline records\tregression\t-1.64\t400.22\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (regression, -1.64%): Stage-local micro-op typedefs do not guarantee a timing win when EX/MEM still carries broad retirement metadata and the split adds payload repacking and routing, so control partitioning must reduce physical fanout rather than only reorganize fields.\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tReset-masked replicated LUTRAM register file\tregression\t-6.53\t380.32\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r8s1 (regression, -6.53%): Reset-masked replicated LUTRAM register files can regress when two full data banks plus per-read valid-bit checks add replication and operand-path control, so distributed-RAM inference must be measured against the compact resettable flop baseline rather than assumed to reduce routing.\nhyp-20260710-002-r9s1\tIsolate divide/remainder in a multi-cycle unit\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r9s1 (broken, n/a): An iterative EX divider must hold one DIV/REM transaction's operands, instruction metadata, and RVFI/forwarding age through start/busy/done and release younger pipeline state only after completion, or all four M-operation checks and `reg_ch0` can fail together.\nhyp-20260710-002-r10s1\tDecouple RVFI metadata from the execute hot path\tregression\t-5.13\t386.0\t\nhyp-20260710-002-r11s1\tSmall direct-mapped write-through data cache\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r11s1 (broken, n/a): A cache integration that instantiates `data_cache` without adding its module to the `rtl/*.sv` build inputs is structurally incomplete and fails cosim before cache performance can be measured.\nhyp-20260710-002-r12s1\tIntegrated direct-mapped data cache\tplacement_failed\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r12s1 (placement_failed, n/a): A 2 KiB direct-mapped cache with explicit tag/data arrays, broad MEM lookup muxing, and a refill FSM can exceed this small FPGA's placement budget, so cache state and miss-control complexity must be physically budgeted before locality gains are measurable.\nhyp-20260710-002-r13s1\tPlacement-bounded tiny data cache\tplacement_failed\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r13s1 (placement_failed, n/a): Shrinking a blocking cache to 256 bytes still failed placement, showing that MEM-boundary tag/data lookup muxing, refill FSM control, and dmem/RVFI fanout can dominate the placement footprint even after cache state is reduced.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The structural history rules out broad buffering/caching and deeper pipelines: the FIFO, elastic queue, store buffer, skid, and both cache sizes either lost IPC/Fmax or failed placement. I’m narrowing the proposal to a low-state pipeline topology change that removes common-path routing without adding speculative metadata or large arrays."}}
