{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '412\\\\.38|source_id|best' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/core.yaml | tail -n 20 && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/core.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/core.yaml:19:  source_id: hyp-20260710-001-r10s0\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:29:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Shared branch compare flag cone\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"EX currently expresses BEQ, BNE, signed, and unsigned relational branches\\nas separate high-level comparisons selected by a branch-op case. That can\\nreplicate comparator logic on the redirect path even though all predicates\\nare functions of the same rs1-rs2 subtraction. CoreMark contains frequent\\nloop and conditional branches, so shortening this control-flow cone may\\nimprove Fmax without adding pipeline latency or changing IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"EX currently expresses BEQ, BNE, signed, and unsigned relational branches\\nas separate high-level comparisons selected by a branch-op case. That can\\nreplicate comparator logic on the redirect path even though all predicates\\nare functions of the same rs1-rs2 subtraction. CoreMark contains frequent\\nloop and conditional branches, so shortening this control-flow cone may\\nimprove Fmax without adding pipeline latency or changing IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the EX branch comparison case with one 33-bit unsigned subtraction\\nthat supplies zero, borrow, and signed-less-than flags. Select BEQ/BNE from\\nthe zero flag and BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU from the corresponding signed or unsigned\\nflag. Preserve the existing branch target adder, redirect priority,\\nmisalignment trap handling, forwarding, and RVFI metadata. Sharing the\\ncomparison flags should reduce duplicated relational/equality cones and\\nfanout on the branch redirect path while leaving all non-branch execution\\nbehavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive all RV32I branch predicates from a shared 33-bit rs1-rs2 subtract flag network while preserving exact signed/unsigned semantics and existing redirect/trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Derive all RV32I branch predicates from a shared 33-bit rs1-rs2 subtract flag network while preserving exact signed/unsigned semantics and existing redirect/trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 412.38, \"delta_pct\": 1.35, \"vs_baseline\": 45.81, \"fmax_mhz\": 185.22, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7500, \"ff\": 1862, \"seeds\": [187.48, 185.22, 174.67], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:03:41.188190Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r10s0 (improvement, +1.35%): A single 33-bit EX subtract with zero, borrow, and overflow-corrected signed-less-than flags can modestly improve CoreMark by sharing BEQ/BNE and signed/unsigned relational branch cones without adding pipeline latency.\"}\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 185.22\n  lut4: 7500\n  ff: 1862\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20260710-001-r10s0\n  updated: '2026-07-10T23:16:13.649774Z'\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
