{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r14s1.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r14s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r14s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Iterative divider sidecar for EX\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The common ALU still elaborates 32-bit division and remainder operators,\n  which can dominate FPGA timing even though CoreMark executes far fewer\n  DIV/REM instructions than ordinary integer and address operations. The\n  previous divider attempt was functionally incomplete, but it identified\n  the right structural opportunity: remove the divider network from the\n  single-cycle EX result cone while paying multi-cycle latency only for the\n  instructions that use it.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU into a 32-cycle restoring divider sidecar\n  behind the EX stage. Capture the complete instruction transaction\n  (operands, signedness, quotient-versus-remainder, destination, and RVFI\n  metadata) when a divide enters EX, hold the younger pipeline state while\n  the unit is busy, and inject exactly one completed result into the normal\n  EX/MEM -> MEM/WB retirement path. Handle divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1\n  overflow as explicit fast terminal cases, preserve forwarding and precise\n  RVFI order, and keep the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions available under\n  the formal define. Removing / and % from the ordinary ALU cone should raise\n  Fmax while the occasional divider stalls remain localized to M-extension\n  traffic.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a resettable 32-step restoring divider with exact RV32M signed, unsigned, divide-by-zero, overflow, quotient, and remainder semantics, plus valid/busy/done handshaking.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove synthesized DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the normal hardware ALU path while retaining the exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS result substitutions and the multiply operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture divider operands and the full in-flight instruction context, hold EX/MEM until completion, and merge the divider result into the existing precise writeback and RVFI metadata path.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add divider request/busy/completion interlocks with explicit priority over younger pipeline movement, while preserving load-use, redirect, dmem-stall, and forward-progress behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the divider sidecar and its completion/hold signals through EX, hazards, forwarding, and retirement without changing the single-channel RVFI or top-level bus contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
