{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r15s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r15s1\ntitle: \"Registered elastic fetch boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current IF/ID path is combinational from io_imemData through instruction\n  decode and the register-file read ports into the ID/EX register. That makes\n  the external instruction bus, decode fanout, and operand routing share one\n  long timing path, even though the pipeline already has valid/stall control.\n  The prior prefetch FIFO was too much front-end state; this targets only the\n  timing boundary and uses a single elastic entry.\nhypothesis: |\n  Insert a registered one-entry IF/ID fetch buffer that captures an instruction\n  and its PC only on an accepted io_imemReady transfer, and let ID consume the\n  buffered entry independently of later imem backpressure. Keep the fetch PC,\n  redirect flush, and valid/ready accounting in the buffer so a redirect\n  invalidates both the buffered wrong-path instruction and any in-flight fetch\n  response. This adds one front-end register boundary but removes the direct\n  imemData-to-decode/regfile timing cone, while sustaining one instruction per\n  cycle once full and preserving precise load-use, RVFI PC flow, and single\n  retirement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the combinational imem-to-ID payload with a one-entry registered fetch buffer carrying PC, instruction, and valid state, including ready-aware capture, consume, redirect flush, and exact PC sequencing.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Adjust the front-end bundle definitions only as needed for the registered valid/ready fetch boundary, retaining all existing retirement metadata and deterministic bubble values.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Reconnect front-end backpressure and redirect control so ID stalls hold the fetch entry, imem stalls do not corrupt it, and redirects cannot allow a stale buffered instruction to retire.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Change instruction-stall generation from raw imemReady gating to fetch-buffer empty/full handshaking while preserving load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect priority.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
