{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Elastic in-order data-memory completion queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current MEM-stage handshake freezes PC, ID/EX, and EX/MEM whenever\n  io_dmemReady is low, so a transient data-bus stall blocks unrelated ALU\n  instructions and directly lowers CoreMark instructions per cycle. The\n  recent fetch FIFO result also shows that buffering only the front end is\n  insufficient when the dominant stall is downstream.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure the memory boundary as a small elastic in-order queue with a\n  dedicated completion/retirement head. Allow younger independent ALU\n  instructions to execute into queue entries while an older load or store\n  waits for io_dmemReady, but prevent younger memory operations from passing\n  an older memory operation and hold dependent consumers until the load data\n  is available. Retire only the queue head, preserving RVFI order, precise\n  traps, register writeback, and architectural memory ordering. This should\n  overlap random dmem backpressure with useful integer work without adding a\n  fetch-time critical path or changing the external bus contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add the metadata needed for elastic memory/completion entries, including age, completion, and deferred load/store state while preserving the existing RVFI payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the single blocking MEM/WB boundary with a small in-order memory/completion queue that holds stalled data requests, accepts younger non-memory results, and exposes only the oldest completed entry to writeback and RVFI.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Generate queue-full, older-memory-order, and load-result dependency stalls instead of freezing the complete pipeline on every dmemReady low cycle.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire elastic queue ready/valid flow through EX, MEM, WB, and retirement so dmem backpressure overlaps independent execution while redirects and RVFI remain precise.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
