{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"ID-stage early control-transfer resolution\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage pipeline currently resolves conditional branches and jumps\n  in EX, flushing younger work and paying a multi-cycle redirect penalty on\n  CoreMark's tight loops. The earlier fetch-prediction experiments added\n  timing and recovery cost on the IF path, so the useful structural opportunity\n  is to shorten the control hazard without decoding branches during fetch.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move legal conditional-branch and jump target/condition resolution into ID\n  with a dedicated PC-plus-immediate adder and comparator. Add decode-stage\n  operand bypasses from EX/MEM and MEM/WB, and conservatively stall only when\n  a branch operand is still waiting on a load or an unresolved producer. Use\n  the early redirect to flush just the younger fetch work, while carrying the\n  resolved next-PC and misalignment-trap metadata into retirement so RVFI,\n  ordering, and illegal-instruction behavior remain unchanged. Removing the\n  branch comparator/target path from EX should reduce taken-loop bubbles\n  without putting instruction decode or target formation on the IF critical\n  path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the ID/EX payload with resolved next-PC and control-transfer fault metadata needed for precise RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment traps.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve legal branches, JAL, and JALR in ID using dedicated target/compare logic and explicit operand bypass inputs, while exporting an early redirect and trap decision.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Prioritize the ID-stage redirect over sequential fetch, coordinate one-cycle flushes with the existing EX and dmem-stall controls, and wire resolved next-PC data to retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add decode-stage dependency checks so branches and JALR wait for unavailable load results while allowing EX/MEM and MEM/WB ALU results to bypass into ID.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the ID-resolved transfer metadata, retain a precise fallback for malformed or misaligned transfers, and remove redundant EX control-transfer work from the timing-critical path.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
