{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.yaml\\\")' && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\", \"title\"=>\"Single-entry nonblocking store buffer\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"motivation\"=>\"The current five-stage pipeline freezes globally whenever an EX/MEM store\\nsees io_dmemReady low, even though a store has no result that younger ALU\\ninstructions need. The prior general completion-queue attempt failed\\nliveness, so a bounded store-only structure is a lower-risk way to overlap\\nthe benchmark's random data-bus stalls without introducing broad out-of-order\\nretirement machinery.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Add a one-entry FIFO store buffer at the MEM boundary. A store is accepted\\ninto the buffer and retires in program order, while the buffer independently\\nholds its address, byte mask, and replicated write data until io_dmemReady\\nacknowledges the write. Allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed\\nbehind a buffered store; keep younger loads ordered by stalling them on a\\npossible store-buffer address conflict, and stop the front end only when the\\nbuffer is full or an older memory-order condition requires it. Keep loads,\\nRVFI fields, redirects, and trap handling on the existing precise path so\\nthis structural change primarily removes store-induced global bubbles.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>5, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\"}]}\nid: hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Single-entry nonblocking store buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage pipeline freezes globally whenever an EX/MEM store\n  sees io_dmemReady low, even though a store has no result that younger ALU\n  instructions need. The prior general completion-queue attempt failed\n  liveness, so a bounded store-only structure is a lower-risk way to overlap\n  the benchmark's random data-bus stalls without introducing broad out-of-order\n  retirement machinery.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry FIFO store buffer at the MEM boundary. A store is accepted\n  into the buffer and retires in program order, while the buffer independently\n  holds its address, byte mask, and replicated write data until io_dmemReady\n  acknowledges the write. Allow younger non-memory instructions to proceed\n  behind a buffered store; keep younger loads ordered by stalling them on a\n  possible store-buffer address conflict, and stop the front end only when the\n  buffer is full or an older memory-order condition requires it. Keep loads,\n  RVFI fields, redirects, and trap handling on the existing precise path so\n  this structural change primarily removes store-induced global bubbles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
