{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r5s1.yaml\\\")' && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r5s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r5s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\", \"title\"=>\"Retimed two-stage execute pipeline\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"motivation\"=>\"The current five-stage pipeline places operand forwarding, a 32-bit ALU,\\nbranch comparison, and control-transfer target formation in one EX cycle.\\nThat wide fan-in and arithmetic cone is a likely remaining Fmax limiter\\nafter the fast-path ALU optimization, while the prior buffering attempts\\nshow that adding queues can cost more IPC than they recover.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Split EX into EX1 and EX2 with a pipeline register between operand\\nselection and execution. EX1 performs source-use-aware forwarding and\\ncaptures the resolved operands and control metadata; EX2 performs the ALU,\\nbranch compare/target calculation, and memory-address generation before the\\nexisting MEM boundary. Add explicit EX1/EX2 bypass priority and interlocks\\nfor the extra latency, and keep redirects, load-use behavior, dmem stalls,\\nand RVFI payloads tied to the same in-order instruction. The added stage\\nshould shorten the critical operand-to-result path enough to raise Fmax\\nwithout the area and ordering overhead of speculative queues.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>6, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Extend the pipeline bundle definitions with an EX1/EX2 execution payload carrying forwarded operands, control, and RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Restructure execute into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/branch/address EX2 stages, with precise redirect and misalignment-trap propagation.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add freshest-writer bypass selection for the retimed EX1/EX2 boundary while preserving load suppression, x0 handling, and EX/MEM priority.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add the one-cycle interlocks and flush/stall precedence required by the extra execute stage, including dmem backpressure and redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Wire the retimed execute stages into MEM/WB, forwarding, hazard control, and RVFI retirement without changing the single-channel top-level contract.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
