{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\\\") | .motivation, .hypothesis, .error' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"The five-stage pipeline currently resolves conditional branches and jumps\nin EX, flushing younger work and paying a multi-cycle redirect penalty on\nCoreMark's tight loops. The earlier fetch-prediction experiments added\ntiming and recovery cost on the IF path, so the useful structural opportunity\nis to shorten the control hazard without decoding branches during fetch.\n\n{\n  \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently resolves conditional branches and jumps\\nin EX, flushing younger work and paying a multi-cycle redirect penalty on\\nCoreMark's tight loops. The earlier fetch-prediction experiments added\\ntiming and recovery cost on the IF path, so the useful structural opportunity\\nis to shorten the control hazard without decoding branches during fetch.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Move legal conditional-branch and jump target/condition resolution into ID\\nwith a dedicated PC-plus-immediate adder and comparator. Add decode-stage\\noperand bypasses from EX/MEM and MEM/WB, and conservatively stall only when\\na branch operand is still waiting on a load or an unresolved producer. Use\\nthe early redirect to flush just the younger fetch work, while carrying the\\nresolved next-PC and misalignment-trap metadata into retirement so RVFI,\\nordering, and illegal-instruction behavior remain unchanged. Removing the\\nbranch comparator/target path from EX should reduce taken-loop bubbles\\nwithout putting instruction decode or target formation on the IF critical\\npath.\\n\",\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 7,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Extend the ID/EX payload with resolved next-PC and control-transfer fault metadata needed for precise RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment traps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Resolve legal branches, JAL, and JALR in ID using dedicated target/compare logic and explicit operand bypass inputs, while exporting an early redirect and trap decision.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Prioritize the ID-stage redirect over sequential fetch, coordinate one-cycle flushes with the existing EX and dmem-stall controls, and wire resolved next-PC data to retirement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add decode-stage dependency checks so branches and JALR wait for unavailable load results while allowing EX/MEM and MEM/WB ALU results to bypass into ID.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Consume the ID-resolved transfer metadata, retain a precise fallback for malformed or misaligned transfers, and remove redundant EX control-transfer work from the timing-critical path.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nformal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\neturncode=0)\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:02 (2)\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY 17:53:00 [insn_sub_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:30  Status: passed\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:31 (31)\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:23 (23)\nSBY 17:53:17 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) 