{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The prior structural attempts show that broad queues and deeper retiming lose to control/IPC overhead. I’m selecting a narrower structural change: a constrained post-MEM completion skid for younger, non-memory ALU results, so dmem backpressure can overlap a small amount of independent work without allowing memory or control-transfer reordering."}}
