{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.category==\\\"structural\\\") | {id,title,outcome,delta_pct,fitness,expected_impact,changes,lesson}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\",\"title\":\"Decoupled instruction prefetch FIFO\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":7.15,\"fitness\":303.05,\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single-PC fetch hold behavior with a four-entry tagged instruction prefetch FIFO, including ready-aware fill, dequeue, redirect flush, and precise PC/valid output.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Reconnect front-end stall and flush handling so downstream hazards only stop FIFO consumption when necessary, while imem backpressure does not freeze already-buffered instructions.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Separate instruction-queue-empty backpressure from imemReady stalls and retain redirect/load-use/dmem stall precedence without allowing duplicate or skipped fetches.\"}],\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r1s1 (regression, +7.15%): A small prefetch FIFO is not automatically beneficial when EX redirects flush every queued instruction and FIFO-empty refill inserts ID bubbles, so redirect frequency and refill cost can outweigh hiding random imem backpressure in CoreMark.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\",\"title\":\"Elastic in-order data-memory completion queue\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":8,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the metadata needed for elastic memory/completion entries, including age, completion, and deferred load/store state while preserving the existing RVFI payload.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single blocking MEM/WB boundary with a small in-order memory/completion queue that holds stalled data requests, accepts younger non-memory results, and exposes only the oldest completed entry to writeback and RVFI.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Generate queue-full, older-memory-order, and load-result dependency stalls instead of freezing the complete pipeline on every dmemReady low cycle.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire elastic queue ready/valid flow through EX, MEM, WB, and retirement so dmem backpressure overlaps independent execution while redirects and RVFI remain precise.\"}],\"lesson\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\",\"title\":\"ID-stage early control-transfer resolution\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":7,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the ID/EX payload with resolved next-PC and control-transfer fault metadata needed for precise RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment traps.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Resolve legal branches, JAL, and JALR in ID using dedicated target/compare logic and explicit operand bypass inputs, while exporting an early redirect and trap decision.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Prioritize the ID-stage redirect over sequential fetch, coordinate one-cycle flushes with the existing EX and dmem-stall controls, and wire resolved next-PC data to retirement.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add decode-stage dependency checks so branches and JALR wait for unavailable load results while allowing EX/MEM and MEM/WB ALU results to bypass into ID.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Consume the ID-resolved transfer metadata, retain a precise fallback for malformed or misaligned transfers, and remove redundant EX control-transfer work from the timing-critical path.\"}],\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): ID-stage branch and jump redirects must latch resolved next-PC and misalignment-trap metadata with the instruction through ID/EX to retirement, because advancing fetch without keeping RVFI `pc_wdata` aligned can fail `pc_fwd` even when instruction checks pass.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\",\"title\":\"Single-entry nonblocking store buffer\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-7.94,\"fitness\":374.56,\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a compact store-buffer entry type carrying valid, address, mask, write data, and RVFI ordering metadata without changing the top-level contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Split store acceptance from external write completion, drive the single buffered request until dmemReady, and expose precise store retirement data while preserving aligned-memory semantics.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the store-buffer ready/full and address-conflict signals so younger independent ALU instructions can flow while a stalled store drains, with in-order retirement and redirect interaction preserved.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace unconditional store-induced pipeline freezing with bounded store-buffer backpressure and conservative load/store ordering checks.\"}],\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (regression, -7.94%): On a single-ported dmem, a one-entry store buffer can lose to its own store-priority arbitration, address-conflict checks, and MEM-stage load-forward path, whose control and conservative ordering stalls outweigh the store bubbles they hide in CoreMark.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\",\"title\":\"Retimed two-stage execute pipeline\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-53.64,\"fitness\":188.61,\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the pipeline bundle definitions with an EX1/EX2 execution payload carrying forwarded operands, control, and RVFI metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Restructure execute into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/branch/address EX2 stages, with precise redirect and misalignment-trap propagation.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add freshest-writer bypass selection for the retimed EX1/EX2 boundary while preserving load suppression, x0 handling, and EX/MEM priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the one-cycle interlocks and flush/stall precedence required by the extra execute stage, including dmem backpressure and redirect recovery.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the retimed execute stages into MEM/WB, forwarding, hazard control, and RVFI retirement without changing the single-channel top-level contract.\"}],\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -53.64%): Retiming EX into EX1/EX2 made dependency, redirect, and dmem-stall interlocks pay extra latency on common in-order paths, so CoreMark IPC loss overwhelmed any Fmax benefit; deeper pipelines need latency-aware bypassing without serializing ALU chains.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\",\"title\":\"Constrained ALU completion skid during data stalls\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define a compact completion-skid payload and valid/age metadata for a younger ALU result while retaining the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the one-entry ALU skid between EX and MEM, select the oldest completed result for writeback, and connect skid forwarding without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose a sideband candidate for non-memory, non-control ALU instructions and prevent skid capture of operations that could redirect, trap, or access memory.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add ordered drain/capture behavior so a blocked older data request remains the retirement head and the younger ALU completion reaches MEM/WB only after it.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace unconditional dmem-stall freezing with skid-full and dependency-aware backpressure, while keeping memory ordering, load-use hazards, redirect flushes, and forward progress precise.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Give the completion skid highest forwarding priority for dependent ALU operands, with x0 and valid gating and older EX/MEM/MEM/WB priority preserved when the skid is absent.\"}],\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): A one-entry ALU completion skid must separate memory completion, skid capture/drain, and EX/MEM clearing while preserving the single MEM/WB retirement slot and age ordering, or `dmemReady` transitions can corrupt CoreMark execution.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
