{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"Stage-local micro-op pipeline records\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage datapath currently carries the full control bundle through\n  every pipeline boundary, including branch, memory, execute, and retirement\n  fields that are irrelevant to most downstream stages. That creates broad\n  control fanout and routing across the EX/MEM and MEM/WB boundaries even\n  though CoreMark is dominated by ordinary ALU and address-generation ops.\n  The prior structural attempts that added queues or pipeline stages paid\n  substantial control and latency cost; a same-depth restructuring can target\n  Fmax without adding retirement or dependency latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Partition the pipeline record into stage-local micro-op controls and a\n  separate retirement metadata payload. Decode still validates the complete\n  RV32IM instruction, but ID/EX latches only execute-relevant controls and\n  operands; EX/MEM forwards only memory/writeback controls plus the RVFI\n  fields needed after execution; and MEM/WB carries only memory-result and\n  retirement state. Remove redundant branch-target bookkeeping and unused\n  control fields from later records, while preserving valid/flush behavior,\n  forwarded source values, precise trap and misalignment metadata, and every\n  RVFI field at the existing single retirement boundary. Narrower stage-local\n  fanout should improve routed Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Replace the monolithic control propagation with compact execute, memory, writeback, and retirement pipeline record types that retain all required RVFI metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Keep the strict legal-instruction decode but expose stage-local control fields instead of requiring the full control bundle to cross every stage.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the compact execute micro-op, operands, immediate, register addresses, and precise retirement metadata at the ID/EX boundary.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the execute-local record and emit only the memory/writeback controls, computed result, and retirement metadata needed by later stages.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use a memory-local record and produce a narrow MEM/WB retirement record, preserving alignment traps, byte masks, load data, and RVFI values.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Reconnect the stage-local records and forwarding/control wiring without changing the top-level IO, single-channel RVFI contract, or retirement ordering.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\", \"title\"=>\"Stage-local micro-op pipeline records\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"motivation\"=>\"The five-stage datapath currently carries the full control bundle through\\nevery pipeline boundary, including branch, memory, execute, and retirement\\nfields that are irrelevant to most downstream stages. That creates broad\\ncontrol fanout and routing across the EX/MEM and MEM/WB boundaries even\\nthough CoreMark is dominated by ordinary ALU and address-generation ops.\\nThe prior structural attempts that added queues or pipeline stages paid\\nsubstantial control and latency cost; a same-depth restructuring can target\\nFmax without adding retirement or dependency latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Partition the pipeline record into stage-local micro-op controls and a\\nseparate retirement metadata payload. Decode still validates the complete\\nRV32IM instruction, but ID/EX latches only execute-relevant controls and\\noperands; EX/MEM forwards only memory/writeback controls plus the RVFI\\nfields needed after execution; and MEM/WB carries only memory-result and\\nretirement state. Remove redundant branch-target bookkeeping and unused\\ncontrol fields from later records, while preserving valid/flush behavior,\\nforwarded source values, precise trap and misalignment metadata, and every\\nRVFI field at the existing single retirement boundary. Narrower stage-local\\nfanout should improve routed Fmax with unchanged CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>3, \"confidence\"=>\"low\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Replace the monolithic control propagation with compact execute, memory, writeback, and retirement pipeline record types that retain all required RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Keep the strict legal-instruction decode but expose stage-local control fields instead of requiring the full control bundle to cross every stage.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Latch the compact execute micro-op, operands, immediate, register addresses, and precise retirement metadata at the ID/EX boundary.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Consume the execute-local record and emit only the memory/writeback controls, computed result, and retirement metadata needed by later stages.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Use a memory-local record and produce a narrow MEM/WB retirement record, preserving alignment traps, byte masks, load data, and RVFI values.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Reconnect the stage-local records and forwarding/control wiring without changing the top-level IO, single-channel RVFI contract, or retirement ordering.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
