{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r10s2.yaml && git diff -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r10s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r10s2\ntitle: \"Atomic target-token loop predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark still pays the EX redirect and wrong-path flush for recurring\n  taken loops. The prior exact-PC predictor was nearly neutral because its\n  IF target mux was combined with an EX table re-lookup and miss repair, and\n  the epoch-qualified variants failed pc_fwd when predictor state changed\n  between fetch and resolution.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny one-entry last-target predictor trained only by retiring taken\n  backward conditional branches. On an IF hit, capture the predicted target\n  atomically with the instruction and use it for the next PC; carry that\n  exact target with the instruction rather than re-reading mutable predictor\n  state in EX. EX suppresses the redirect only when the captured target,\n  resolved taken target, and alignment all agree. Any loop exit, alias, table\n  replacement, or stale prediction therefore follows the normal redirect\n  path, while eliminating the EX re-lookup and epoch-sensitive acceptance\n  logic from the prior attempts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an atomic prediction-valid bit and captured predicted-next-PC field to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, with zeroed bubble values.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a reset-safe one-entry exact-PC backward-loop target predictor with retirement-only training and a combinational IF lookup.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the predictor hit to select the next fetch PC and capture the exact target alongside the fetched instruction, preserving redirect, stall, and reset priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pipeline the immutable prediction token and captured target with the owning instruction, clearing both on flushes and bubbles.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate predictions solely from the captured target and current resolved branch result, suppressing only an exact aligned taken match and repairing all mismatches precisely.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect predictor lookup and retirement training while keeping RVFI pc_wdata, retirement order, and single-channel behavior unchanged.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
