{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r11s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Committed return-only stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The previous BTFNT, BTB, and loop-target predictors paid more IF timing,\n  metadata routing, and recovery cost than their saved conditional-branch\n  redirects were worth. CoreMark still has frequent call/return control flow,\n  so a narrowly scoped indirect-return predictor is a better area/timing\n  tradeoff than another general target table.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a two-entry committed return-address stack that predicts only canonical\n  JALR returns using x1/x5, with calls pushing pc+4 and returns popping only at\n  retirement. Keep predictor state non-speculative: no checkpoints, epochs, or\n  updates from flushed instructions. Carry only a compact return prediction\n  token and validate the captured target against the resolved JALR target and\n  the owning instruction PC; any miss, alias, non-return JALR, stall, or\n  misaligned target takes the existing precise redirect/recovery path. This\n  should remove recurring return flushes while limiting IF lookup and control\n  fanout to indirect-return sites instead of burdening every branch.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a reset-safe two-entry committed return-address stack, canonical call/return classification, IF lookup, and retirement-only push/pop updates.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact return-prediction-valid, target, and owning-PC token fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles, with deterministic bubble values.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the return-only lookup to select a predicted fetch target while preserving imemReady, reset, redirect priority, and sequential fallback.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pipeline the immutable return prediction token with its instruction and clear it on bubbles or flushes.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate a return prediction against the resolved JALR target and instruction PC, suppressing redirects only for exact aligned matches and repairing all misses.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect prediction lookup, EX validation, and retirement push/pop training without changing the single-channel RVFI contract or order.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
