{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r12s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Selective decode-stage branch prediction\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The bench core resolves conditional branches in EX, so taken CoreMark\n  loops pay the full redirect and flush penalty. Prior BTFNT, BTB, loop,\n  and return predictors showed that fetch-side tables and prediction tokens\n  add more timing and recovery cost than they save. A selective predictor\n  that handles only easy conditional branches in ID can remove the common\n  loop penalty without placing instruction decode or a target table on the\n  ordinary IF path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a zero-state decode-stage conditional-branch predictor/resolver. For a\n  legal conditional branch whose source operands are available through the\n  existing register-file/WB path, compute its exact direction and target in\n  ID and redirect the PC at the ID/EX capture edge; carry the resolved\n  next-PC and aligned/misaligned status with that branch so RVFI pc_wdata is\n  exact. If either operand is an unresolved producer, or if the instruction\n  is JAL/JALR or otherwise uncertain, suppress the early prediction and use\n  the existing EX resolution and forwarding path. This should reduce taken\n  loop bubbles while avoiding speculative state, broad IF prediction\n  metadata, and unsafe recovery on stalls or misaligned transfers.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact ID-resolved-branch and next-PC metadata to the pipeline bundles, with deterministic bubble values for precise RVFI retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve only dependency-safe legal conditional branches in ID using the existing register values and a local target/compare cone, and emit an early redirect plus aligned-target fault metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate early branch resolution on producer availability, stalling or falling back to EX for unresolved operands without weakening load-use or dmem-stall ordering.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Prioritize the precise ID branch redirect, connect its metadata through retirement, and retain the existing EX redirect as the fallback for all non-predicted transfers.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume ID-resolved conditional-branch metadata without issuing a duplicate redirect, while preserving EX forwarding, fallback resolution, and misalignment trap behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
