after the\\ntarget has been observed. IF performs just a tag compare and target mux,\\nwith no opcode or immediate decode; the instruction carries a compact\\nprediction token plus predictor epoch, while EX revalidates the same entry\\nand suppresses its redirect only for an epoch-matched taken target. A\\npredicted loop exit redirects to the fall-through path and invalidates the\\nentry at retirement. Epoch-qualified lookup and retirement-only training\\nkeep replacement, stalls, flushes, RVFI pc_wdata, and wrong-path state from\\ncreating the pc_fwd failure seen in the earlier loop-target cache.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact loop-prediction valid/epoch fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX records without carrying a predicted 32-bit target through the pipeline.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement the one-entry exact-PC backward-loop target state, IF tag/target lookup, epoch tracking, EX revalidation, and retirement-only taken/exit training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use an epoch-qualified predictor hit to select the next fetch PC while preserving imemReady, redirect, reset, and flush priority and emitting an atomic prediction token.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pipeline the prediction token and captured epoch with its owning instruction, clearing them on bubbles and redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the prediction token and epoch-qualified predictor hit with the resolved branch next PC, suppressing only an agreeing taken-loop redirect and repairing all mismatches precisely.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect predictor lookup, EX validation, and MEM/WB retirement training without changing the single-channel RVFI contract or retirement ordering.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 