{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r13s2.yaml\nruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r13s2.yaml\\\")[\\\"id\\\"]'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Zero-token unconditional JAL folding\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The bench pipeline currently lets every JAL reach EX before redirecting,\n  paying the same front-end recovery cost as a conditional branch even though\n  a JAL target is known exactly from the fetched instruction. Earlier BTB,\n  loop, RAS, and ID-branch predictors added prediction metadata or compare\n  logic to common paths and lost more Fmax than their saved redirects earned.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a certainty-only front-end predictor for unconditional JAL. When IF has\n  a valid JAL and its immediate target is aligned, form that target locally\n  and advance the fetch PC directly, so the target instruction enters the\n  pipeline without waiting for the JAL's EX redirect. Do not add a predictor\n  table, history state, prediction-valid token, or EX agreement mux: JAL is\n  always taken, while misaligned targets fall back to the existing EX trap\n  path. Keep conditional branches, JALR, bus stalls, forwarding, RVFI\n  pc_wdata, and retirement ordering on their existing paths. The narrow scope\n  should remove call/jump bubbles without burdening ordinary ALU fetches with\n  branch-history or target-table fanout.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize valid JAL instructions, generate an aligned J-immediate target in IF, and fold the fetch PC to that target while retaining reset, imemReady, redirect, and misalignment fallback behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Treat aligned JAL redirects as already folded by IF while retaining JAL PC+4 writeback, pc_next metadata, and the existing precise redirect/trap behavior for non-folded or misaligned transfers.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Coordinate JAL folding with imem and dmem stalls so a folded target is accepted only when the target fetch is valid and no younger wrong-path instruction can advance.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the fold-valid control between IF, EX, and hazard logic without changing the single-channel RVFI interface or retirement order.\"\n\"hyp-20260710-003-r13s2\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
