{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r14s2.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])[\\\"id\\\"]' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r14s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"Zero-state early canonical return prediction\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Canonical function returns are unconditional control transfers, but the\n  current pipeline waits until EX to add the return-register value and then\n  flushes the younger fetch/decode work. Earlier table-based BTBs and RAS\n  designs paid substantial timing and recovery overhead on ordinary fetches.\n  A targeted return predictor can use the already-read x1/x5 value without\n  predictor state or aliasing.\nhypothesis: |\n  Resolve only canonical returns (JALR with rd=x0, rs1=x1 or x5, and a zero\n  immediate) in ID when the source value is available from the register file\n  or existing WB bypass. Form the exact aligned target there and redirect the\n  fetch PC one stage early, carrying a compact early-return token and target\n  through ID/EX so EX suppresses only the matching normal redirect. If the\n  source has an unresolved producer, the target is misaligned, or the\n  instruction is not canonical, retain the existing EX path. This removes\n  recurring return bubbles while avoiding a BTB, RAS checkpoints, history,\n  or prediction logic on non-return instructions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact early-return target and valid metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with deterministic bubble values.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize only legal canonical x1/x5 JALR returns, use the existing register-file/WB-visible operand, and generate an aligned early redirect target without adding predictor state.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Suppress early-return resolution when the return register has an unresolved producer, while preserving load-use, imem, dmem, and redirect priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the ID return redirect and compact metadata through the front end and retirement control without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate the captured early-return target against the normal JALR result, suppress only an exact aligned match, and retain precise fallback and trap behavior.\"\n\"hyp-20260710-003-r14s2\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
