ken, n/a): A fetch-side return hint must be canceled or repaired for a resolved misaligned JALR, because EX suppressing the trap redirect after IF already advanced to the predicted target violates RVFI `pc_fwd`.\"}\n35:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently inserts a full bubble whenever the\\ninstruction immediately after a load consumes its result, even though the\\ncombinational MEM-stage load extraction already has the returned word in\\nthe same cycle. CoreMark has a dense mix of loads followed by address,\\ncompare, and loop-body operations, so these conservative interlocks reduce\\nretired instructions per cycle independently of Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently inserts a full bubble whenever the\\ninstruction immediately after a load consumes its result, even though the\\ncombinational MEM-stage load extraction already has the returned word in\\nthe same cycle. CoreMark has a dense mix of loads followed by address,\\ncompare, and loop-body operations, so these conservative interlocks reduce\\nretired instructions per cycle independently of Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a precise MEM-to-EX load-result bypass that forwards the sign- or\\nzero-extended load value directly from mem_stage into the EX operand mux.\\nSuppress the load-use bubble only when the load response is ready and the\\naccess is legal; retain the existing stall when dmemReady is low and retain\\nnormal trap behavior for misaligned loads. Give this bypass priority over\\nMEM/WB forwarding, carry the forwarded operands into the existing EX/MEM\\nRVFI fields, and leave retirement order, memory masks, and all RV32M paths\\nunchanged. This should improve CoreMark IPC without adding a new pipeline\\nstage or speculative state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the already-computed load extraction result and a legal-load forward-valid signal without changing dmem handshakes, alignment traps, or RVFI capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a highest-priority MEM load-data forwarding selection while retaining freshest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the MEM load bypass in the EX operand muxes and latch the resulting operands for architectural execution and RVFI source data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate only the load-use bubble on the legal, ready MEM bypass; continue freezing the pipeline for dmem stalls and trapping accesses.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire mem_stage load-forward data and validity through forwarding and hazard control while preserving the single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the already-computed load extraction result and a legal-load forward-valid signal without changing dmem handshakes, alignment traps, or RVFI capture.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a highest-priority MEM load-data forwarding selection while retaining freshest-writer priority and x0 suppression.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the MEM load bypass in the EX operand muxes and latch the resulting operands for architectural execution and RVFI source data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate only the load-use bubble on the legal, ready MEM bypass; continue freezing the pipeline for dmem stalls and trapping accesses.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire mem_stage load-forward data and validity through forwarding and hazard control while preserving the single-channel RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 246.44, \"delta_pct\": -40.24, \"vs_baseline\": -12.86, \"fmax_mhz\": 106.5, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4321614, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7592, \"ff\": 1861, \"seeds\": [106.5, 93.57, 109.79], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:47:35.047886Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r12s0 (regression, -40.24%): Same-cycle MEM-to-EX load forwarding pulled dmem-ready/load-legality control and an extra bypass mux into common EX operand and redirect paths, so removing load-use bubbles did not repay the added timing cost in CoreMark.\"}\n37:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Selective decode-stage branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench core resolves conditional branches in EX, so taken CoreMark\\nloops pay the full redirect and flush penalty. Prior BTFNT, BTB, loop,\\nand return predictors showed that fetch-side tables and prediction tokens\\nadd more timing and recovery cost than they save. A selective predictor\\nthat handles only easy conditional branches in ID can remove the common\\nloop penalty without placing instruction decode or a target table on the\\nordinary IF path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core resolves conditional branches in EX, so taken CoreMark\\nloops pay the full redirect and flush penalty. Prior BTFNT, BTB, loop,\\nand return predictors showed that fetch-side tables and prediction tokens\\nadd more timing and recovery cost than they save. A selective predictor\\nthat handles only easy conditional branches in ID can remove the common\\nloop penalty without placing instruction decode or a target table on the\\nordinary IF path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a zero-state decode-stage conditional-branch predictor/resolver. For a\\nlegal conditional branch whose source operands are available through the\\nexisting register-file/WB path, compute its exact direction and target in\\nID and redirect the PC at the ID/EX capture edge; carry the resolved\\nnext-PC and aligned/misaligned status with that branch so RVFI pc_wdata is\\nexact. If either operand is an unresolved producer, or if the instruction\\nis JAL/JALR or otherwise uncertain, suppress the early prediction and use\\nthe existing EX resolution and forwarding path. This should reduce taken\\nloop bubbles while avoiding speculative state, broad IF prediction\\nmetadata, and unsafe recovery on stalls or misaligned transfers.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact ID-resolved-branch and next-PC metadata to the pipeline bundles, with deterministic bubble values for precise RVFI retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve only dependency-safe legal conditional branches in ID using the existing register values and a local target/compare cone, and emit an early redirect plus aligned-target fault metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate early branch resolution on producer availability, stalling or falling back to EX for unresolved operands without weakening load-use or dmem-stall ordering.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Prioritize the precise ID branch redirect, connect its metadata through retirement, and retain the existing EX redirect as the fallback for all non-predicted transfers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume ID-resolved conditional-branch metadata without issuing a duplicate redirect, while preserving EX forwarding, fallback resolution, and misalignment trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact ID-resolved-branch and next-PC metadata to the pipeline bundles, with deterministic bubble values for precise RVFI retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve only dependency-safe legal conditional branches in ID using the existing register values and a local target/compare cone, and emit an early redirect plus aligned-target fault metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate early branch resolution on producer availability, stalling or falling back to EX for unresolved operands without weakening load-use or dmem-stall ordering.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Prioritize the precise ID branch redirect, connect its metadata through retirement, and retain the existing EX redirect as the fallback for all non-predicted transfers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume ID-resolved conditional-branch metadata without issuing a duplicate redirect, while preserving EX forwarding, fallback resolution, and misalignment trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 320.8, \"delta_pct\": -22.21, \"vs_baseline\": 13.43, \"fmax_mhz\": 138.01, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4302006, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7976, \"ff\": 1925, \"seeds\": [137.91, 138.01, 142.76], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:49:39.945493Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r12s2 (regression, -22.21%): A selective ID-stage branch resolver can still regress CoreMark when its duplicate branch compare/target arithmetic, ID/EX resolution metadata, and redirect-versus-stall arbitration add common-path control and routing that outweigh the taken-loop bubbles removed.\"}\n38:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r13s0\", \"title\": \"Narrow post-EX control payload\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage core carries the full decode control record through both\\nEX/MEM and MEM/WB even though ALU selection, branch classification, and\\njump classification are no longer consumed after EX. Those dead fields add\\nflip-flops, routing, and control fanout around the common memory and\\nwriteback paths, where an IPC-neutral timing improvement is especially\\nvaluable on the small Tang Nano device.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage core carries the full decode control record through both\\nEX/MEM and MEM/WB even though ALU selection, branch classification, and\\njump classification are no longer consumed after EX. Those dead fields add\\nflip-flops, routing, and control fanout around the common memory and\\nwriteback paths, where an IPC-neutral timing improvement is especially\\nvaluable on the small Tang Nano device.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Introduce a compact post-EX memory/writeback control record containing only\\nmemory read/write, width/sign extension, register-write, load-select, and\\nillegal/trap bits. Pack this reduced record into EX/MEM and MEM/WB while\\nmapping the existing decoded controls into it at the EX boundary. Keep all\\nEX branch, jump, ALU, and forwarding behavior unchanged, and preserve the\\nexact memory masks, misalignment traps, RVFI fields, writeback selection,\\nand single-cycle retirement semantics. Removing the unused control-flow\\nfields from the broad pipeline bundles should reduce post-EX routing and\\nimprove Fmax without adding bubbles or speculative state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact post-EX memory/writeback control typedef and use it in EX/MEM and MEM/WB instead of carrying the full decode control record.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Translate the validated EX control record into the reduced post-EX control fields while preserving jump results, misalignment traps, and all existing forwarding and retirement metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume and pipeline the reduced control record without changing dmem handshakes, byte masks, load extension, RVFI reporting, or writeback behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact post-EX memory/writeback control typedef and use it in EX/MEM and MEM/WB instead of carrying the full decode control record.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Translate the validated EX control record into the reduced post-EX control fields while preserving jump results, misalignment traps, and all existing forwarding and retirement metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume and pipeline the reduced control record without changing dmem handshakes, byte masks, load extension, RVFI reporting, or writeback behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 381.23, \"delta_pct\": -7.55, \"vs_baseline\": 34.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 171.23, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7501, \"ff\": 1863, \"seeds\": [153.7, 171.23, 174.52], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:01:49.126677Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 13}\n39:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Placement-bounded tiny data cache\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current blocking MEM boundary sends every normal-RAM access through the\\nexternally stalled dmem port. The previous 2 KiB cache direction was\\nplacement_failed, so the next structural attempt should preserve locality\\nbenefits while using a deliberately small state and control footprint.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current blocking MEM boundary sends every normal-RAM access through the\\nexternally stalled dmem port. The previous 2 KiB cache direction was\\nplacement_failed, so the next structural attempt should preserve locality\\nbenefits while using a deliberately small state and control footprint.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Integrate a 256-byte direct-mapped, four-word-line write-through cache in\\nthe MEM boundary, with only sixteen lines of tag/valid/data state. Aligned\\nnormal-RAM loads should return on a hit without consulting io_dmemReady;\\nmisses should hold the oldest request and refill one line in order, while\\nstores update a hit line and remain write-through with no-write-allocate on\\na miss. Bypass UART and marker MMIO, perform alignment traps before lookup,\\nand keep the existing single MEM/WB retirement and RVFI reporting. The\\nreduced array and narrow miss FSM should fit the FPGA placement budget while\\nremoving repeated CoreMark working-set accesses from the random dmem-stall\\npath.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a 16-line, four-word-line write-through cache directly at the MEM boundary, including reset-safe valid/tag/data state, hit handling, serialized refill, MMIO bypass, byte masks, alignment traps, and unchanged RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire cache hit, miss, and transaction-busy status through the existing MEM/WB and forwarding paths without changing the top-level IO or single-retirement contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace raw dmemReady gating with cache transaction busy/complete gating so hits proceed without a pipeline stall while misses and write-through operations hold the in-flight memory instruction exactly once.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a 16-line, four-word-line write-through cache directly at the MEM boundary, including reset-safe valid/tag/data state, hit handling, serialized refill, MMIO bypass, byte masks, alignment traps, and unchanged RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire cache hit, miss, and transaction-busy status through the existing MEM/WB and forwarding paths without changing the top-level IO or single-retirement contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace raw dmemReady gating with cache transaction busy/complete gating so hits proceed without a pipeline stall while misses and write-through operations hold the in-flight memory instruction exactly once.\"}], \"outcome\": \"placement_failed\", \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": \"placement_failed\", \"seeds\": [null, null, null], \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r13s1 (placement_failed, n/a): Shrinking a blocking cache to 256 bytes still failed placement, showing that MEM-boundary tag/data lookup muxing, refill FSM control, and dmem/RVFI fanout can dominate the placement footprint even after cache state is reduced.\"}\n40:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Zero-token unconditional JAL folding\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench pipeline currently lets every JAL reach EX before redirecting,\\npaying the same front-end recovery cost as a conditional branch even though\\na JAL target is known exactly from the fetched instruction. Earlier BTB,\\nloop, RAS, and ID-branch predictors added prediction metadata or compare\\nlogic to common paths and lost more Fmax than their saved redirects earned.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench pipeline currently lets every JAL reach EX before redirecting,\\npaying the same front-end recovery cost as a conditional branch even though\\na JAL target is known exactly from the fetched instruction. Earlier BTB,\\nloop, RAS, and ID-branch predictors added prediction metadata or compare\\nlogic to common paths and lost more Fmax than their saved redirects earned.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a certainty-only front-end predictor for unconditional JAL. When IF has\\na valid JAL and its immediate target is aligned, form that target locally\\nand advance the fetch PC directly, so the target instruction enters the\\npipeline without waiting for the JAL's EX redirect. Do not add a predictor\\ntable, history state, prediction-valid token, or EX agreement mux: JAL is\\nalways taken, while misaligned targets fall back to the existing EX trap\\npath. Keep conditional branches, JALR, bus stalls, forwarding, RVFI\\npc_wdata, and retirement ordering on their existing paths. The narrow scope\\nshould remove call/jump bubbles without burdening ordinary ALU fetches with\\nbranch-history or target-table fanout.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid JAL instructions, generate an aligned J-immediate target in IF, and fold the fetch PC to that target while retaining reset, imemReady, redirect, and misalignment fallback behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat aligned JAL redirects as already folded by IF while retaining JAL PC+4 writeback, pc_next metadata, and the existing precise redirect/trap behavior for non-folded or misaligned transfers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate JAL folding with imem and dmem stalls so a folded target is accepted only when the target fetch is valid and no younger wrong-path instruction can advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the fold-valid control between IF, EX, and hazard logic without changing the single-channel RVFI interface or retirement order.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize valid JAL instructions, generate an aligned J-immediate target in IF, and fold the fetch PC to that target while retaining reset, imemReady, redirect, and misalignment fallback behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat aligned JAL redirects as already folded by IF while retaining JAL PC+4 writeback, pc_next metadata, and the existing precise redirect/trap behavior for non-folded or misaligned transfers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Coordinate JAL folding with imem and dmem stalls so a folded target is accepted only when the target fetch is valid and no younger wrong-path instruction can advance.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the fold-valid control between IF, EX, and hazard logic without changing the single-channel RVFI interface or retirement order.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 377.76, \"delta_pct\": -8.4, \"vs_baseline\": 33.57, \"fmax_mhz\": 167.81, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4442217, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7617, \"ff\": 1865, \"seeds\": [167.81, 166.03, 170.27], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:05:15.630507Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13}\n41:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r14s0\", \"title\": \"Share EX PC-plus-four result path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline recomputes the sequential PC-plus-four value in\\nmultiple EX/MEM assignments: it feeds JAL/JALR link writeback and also\\nsupplies pc_wdata for ordinary instructions and precise transfer traps.\\nThis is a small but always-present adder/mux cone adjacent to the existing\\nbranch and jump resolution logic, where an IPC-neutral timing improvement\\nis preferable to another predictor or memory structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline recomputes the sequential PC-plus-four value in\\nmultiple EX/MEM assignments: it feeds JAL/JALR link writeback and also\\nsupplies pc_wdata for ordinary instructions and precise transfer traps.\\nThis is a small but always-present adder/mux cone adjacent to the existing\\nbranch and jump resolution logic, where an IPC-neutral timing improvement\\nis preferable to another predictor or memory structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Factor one explicitly shared EX pc_plus4 signal and use it for every\\nreturn-address and sequential pc_next selection, while retaining separate\\nbranch and JALR target arithmetic and the current redirect/trap priority.\\nThe change should let synthesis place one dedicated PC incrementer and\\nreduce duplicated adder outputs and mux fanout without adding a pipeline\\nstage, changing forwarding, or carrying any new prediction metadata.\\nMisaligned branch/jump traps must continue to report pc_plus4 and suppress\\nthe redirect exactly as before.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Create one shared pc_plus4 expression and use it consistently for JAL/JALR link data, sequential pc_next, and misalignment-trap recovery while preserving existing target and redirect behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Create one shared pc_plus4 expression and use it consistently for JAL/JALR link data, sequential pc_next, and misalignment-trap recovery while preserving existing target and redirect behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 392.52, \"delta_pct\": -4.82, \"vs_baseline\": 38.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 176.3, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7495, \"ff\": 1870, \"seeds\": [163.56, 178.83, 176.3], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Implementation notes\\n\\n- Changed `cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv` to define one shared `pc_plus4` signal\\n  (`in.pc + 32'd4`). JAL/JALR link data, ordinary sequential `pc_next`, and\\n  misalignment-trap recovery now all use that signal.\\n- Branch-target and JALR-target arithmetic, redirect suppression, and trap\\n  control behavior were left unchanged.\\n- No deviation from the hypothesis and no implementation concerns identified.\\n- Ordered Verilator lint passed with `core_pkg.sv` first, as required by the\\n  RTL source comments. The exact wildcard command reports pre-existing\\n  source-order typedef errors because it presents `core.sv` before\\n  `core_pkg.sv`.\\n- Local formal status: blocked before check generation. `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl\\n  CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` reached staging but the sandbox\\n  denied cleanup/writes under `formal/riscv-formal` with `Operation not\\n  permitted`; no formal counterexample was produced.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:13:47.288540Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r14s0 (regression, -4.82%): Explicitly factoring a shared EX `pc_plus4` for link data, sequential `pc_next`, and misalignment recovery regressed CoreMark, suggesting that tiny always-present arithmetic should be changed only when synthesis evidence shows a net timing or resource benefit.\"}\n43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Zero-state early canonical return prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Canonical function returns are unconditional control transfers, but the\\ncurrent pipeline waits until EX to add the return-register value and then\\nflushes the younger fetch/decode work. Earlier table-based BTBs and RAS\\ndesigns paid substantial timing and recovery overhead on ordinary fetches.\\nA targeted return predictor can use the already-read x1/x5 value without\\npredictor state or aliasing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Canonical function returns are unconditional control transfers, but the\\ncurrent pipeline waits until EX to add the return-register value and then\\nflushes the younger fetch/decode work. Earlier table-based BTBs and RAS\\ndesigns paid substantial timing and recovery overhead on ordinary fetches.\\nA targeted return predictor can use the already-read x1/x5 value without\\npredictor state or aliasing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Resolve only canonical returns (JALR with rd=x0, rs1=x1 or x5, and a zero\\nimmediate) in ID when the source value is available from the register file\\nor existing WB bypass. Form the exact aligned target there and redirect the\\nfetch PC one stage early, carrying a compact early-return token and target\\nthrough ID/EX so EX suppresses only the matching normal redirect. If the\\nsource has an unresolved producer, the target is misaligned, or the\\ninstruction is not canonical, retain the existing EX path. This removes\\nrecurring return bubbles while avoiding a BTB, RAS checkpoints, history,\\nor prediction logic on non-return instructions.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact early-return target and valid metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with deterministic bubble values.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only legal canonical x1/x5 JALR returns, use the existing register-file/WB-visible operand, and generate an aligned early redirect target without adding predictor state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress early-return resolution when the return register has an unresolved producer, while preserving load-use, imem, dmem, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the ID return redirect and compact metadata through the front end and retirement control without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Validate the captured early-return target against the normal JALR result, suppress only an exact aligned match, and retain precise fallback and trap behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact early-return target and valid metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with deterministic bubble values.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize only legal canonical x1/x5 JALR returns, use the existing register-file/WB-visible operand, and generate an aligned early redirect target without adding predictor state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress early-return resolution when the return register has an unresolved producer, while preserving load-use, imem, dmem, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the ID return redirect and compact metadata through the front end and retirement control without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Validate the captured early-return target against the normal JALR result, suppress only an exact aligned match, and retain precise fallback and trap behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 288.02, \"delta_pct\": -30.16, \"vs_baseline\": 1.84, \"fmax_mhz\": 128.98, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4478185, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7672, \"ff\": 1919, \"seeds\": [142.59, 124.04, 128.98], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:17:40.952246Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r14s2 (regression, -30.16%): Zero-state ID-stage canonical-return prediction can regress CoreMark when ID/EX and EX/MEM source-readiness comparators plus early-redirect/token plumbing burden common decode and recovery paths more than the occasional EX return flush costs.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
