{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"predictor\\\") | [.id, .title, .outcome, (.delta_pct|tostring), (.fitness|tostring), (.fmax_mhz|tostring), (.lesson // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\tFetch-time backward-taken branch prediction\tregression\t23.25\t348.58\t150.22\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, +23.25%): A fetch-time BTFNT predictor can lose badly when `imem_data` branch decode, immediate formation, target addition, and prediction metadata extend the PC/IF critical path and recovery overhead enough to outweigh saved backward-loop redirects in CoreMark.\nhyp-20260710-003-r2s2\tPC-indexed learned branch target buffer\tbroken\tnull\tnull\tnull\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (broken, n/a): A PC-indexed BTB must carry prediction-valid/next-PC metadata atomically with the fetched instruction and reconcile it with EX `resolved_next_pc` and RVFI `pc_wdata`, or redirect recovery can break `pc_fwd` even when instruction checks pass.\nhyp-20260710-003-r3s2\tDecode-stage return-address stack predictor\tregression\t-63.7\t147.68\t66.33\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r3s2 (regression, -63.70%): Decode-stage RAS prediction can lose badly when speculative push/pop checkpoints, recovery control, and carried predicted-PC metadata add ID/EX/EX muxing and fanout that cost more than the saved JALR return flushes in CoreMark.\nhyp-20260710-003-r4s2\tTiny fully tagged last-target predictor\tbroken\tnull\tnull\tnull\t\nhyp-20260710-003-r5s2\tConfidence-qualified tiny tagged BTB\tregression\t-24.58\t306.85\t132.05\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (regression, -24.58%): Even confidence-gating a two-entry tagged BTB can regress CoreMark when every fetched instruction carries `predicted_valid`/`predicted_next_pc` through ID/EX and pays IF next-PC selection plus EX resolved-next-PC comparison and flush-repair overhead for a small number of saved loop redirects.\nhyp-20260710-003-r6s2\tTokenized exact-PC loop target predictor\tregression\t-1.34\t401.44\t173.55\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (regression, -1.34%): Even a one-entry exact-PC target table with only a one-bit pipeline token can regress CoreMark when IF target selection plus EX re-lookup/agreement and miss-repair redirects cost more than the repeatedly taken loop flushes it removes.\nhyp-20260710-003-r7s2\tAligned JAL early-target predictor\tregression\t-6.48\t380.51\t169.03\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r7s2 (regression, -6.48%): Even a zero-state aligned-JAL predictor can regress CoreMark when IF-side J-immediate formation and target addition lengthen the fetch path and the carried prediction token plus EX agreement check add recovery/control overhead that outweighs saved JAL flushes.\nhyp-20260710-003-r8s2\tRetirement-trained loop target cache\tbroken\tnull\tnull\tnull\t\nhyp-20260710-003-r9s2\tEpoch-qualified one-entry loop predictor\tbroken\tnull\tnull\tnull\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r9s2 (broken, n/a): An epoch-qualified loop-prediction token is unsafe unless EX compares its epoch with the live predictor entry; checking only `loop_pred_entry_valid` and target can suppress a required redirect after replacement or flush and violate RVFI `pc_fwd`.\nhyp-20260710-003-r10s2\tAtomic target-token loop predictor\tregression\t-39.27\t247.09\t106.54\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r10s2 (regression, -39.27%): Making a one-entry loop target immutable with the instruction does not make prediction profitable when every hit still drives an IF next-PC mux and IF/ID/EX token path, while alias or stale hits require EX repair redirects that outweigh saved CoreMark loop flushes.\nhyp-20260710-003-r11s2\tCommitted return-only stack predictor\tbroken\tnull\tnull\tnull\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r11s2 (broken, n/a): A fetch-side return hint must be canceled or repaired for a resolved misaligned JALR, because EX suppressing the trap redirect after IF already advanced to the predicted target violates RVFI `pc_fwd`.\nhyp-20260710-003-r12s2\tSelective decode-stage branch prediction\tregression\t-22.21\t320.8\t138.01\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r12s2 (regression, -22.21%): A selective ID-stage branch resolver can still regress CoreMark when its duplicate branch compare/target arithmetic, ID/EX resolution metadata, and redirect-versus-stall arbitration add common-path control and routing that outweigh the taken-loop bubbles removed.\nhyp-20260710-003-r13s2\tZero-token unconditional JAL folding\tregression\t-8.4\t377.76\t167.81\t\nhyp-20260710-003-r14s2\tZero-state early canonical return prediction\tregression\t-30.16\t288.02\t128.98\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r14s2 (regression, -30.16%): Zero-state ID-stage canonical-return prediction can regress CoreMark when ID/EX and EX/MEM source-readiness comparators plus early-redirect/token plumbing burden common decode and recovery paths more than the occasional EX return flush costs.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
