{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml && git diff -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Decode-stage return-address stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark performs frequent function calls and returns, while the current\n  core resolves JAL/JALR in EX and pays a redirect flush on every return.\n  Earlier IF-stage BTFNT and BTB attempts either lengthened the fetch path or\n  broke pc_fwd, so a predictor should target the high-value JALR-return case\n  without adding instruction decode and target arithmetic to IF.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small speculative return-address stack and perform return prediction\n  in ID for canonical JALR returns (x1/x5 link register, zero immediate).\n  Track call pushes and return pops with a shadow/speculative stack, carry an\n  explicit predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid bit through the pipeline,\n  and compare the prediction with EX's resolved next PC. On a mismatch, EX\n  must redirect and restore the stack metadata so RVFI pc_wdata, ordering,\n  traps, and arbitrary symbolic instruction streams remain precise. Keeping\n  the lookup in ID confines the added muxing to the existing decode path while\n  removing return redirect bubbles on repeated CoreMark call sites.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and return-stack action metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize canonical calls and returns, query the small return-address stack in decode, and pipeline prediction metadata without changing the architectural decode legality defaults.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept an early decode-stage predicted target with correct priority relative to reset, bus stalls, and EX recovery redirects, while retaining sequential fetch when the stack has no valid entry.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the carried return prediction against the resolved JAL/JALR next PC, generate precise recovery redirects, and expose committed call/return outcomes for stack repair.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire decode prediction and resolved recovery/training signals through the pipeline so only correctly predicted returns avoid the existing EX redirect flush.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
