{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]).slice(\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"changes\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Tiny fully tagged last-target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Taken-loop redirects are still paid in EX, but the earlier BTFNT and RAS\n  experiments showed that fetch-time instruction decoding and speculative\n  stack bookkeeping can cost more timing and area than they save. A single\n  fully tagged entry can learn the hot target of the most recently taken\n  control-transfer PC with substantially less state and no dependence on\n  imemData in the fetch critical path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry last-target branch buffer indexed by an exact full-PC tag.\n  On a hit, fetch advances directly to the recorded target while the\n  current instruction carries prediction-valid and predicted-next-PC bits\n  through ID/EX. Train the entry only from a valid EX-resolved taken branch,\n  JAL, or JALR; invalidate it when a matching conditional branch resolves\n  not-taken. EX compares the carried prediction with the resolved next PC,\n  suppressing the normal redirect on a hit and redirecting plus flushing on\n  every miss. This preserves precise RVFI pc_wdata and recovery while\n  avoiding fetch-time opcode/immediate decode and limiting predictor muxing\n  to one tag compare and target mux.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement the one-entry fully tagged last-target buffer, including exact-PC lookup, taken-transfer training, matching not-taken invalidation, and reset state.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Give fetch a predicted target input with imemReady and EX-redirect priority, advancing on a valid predictor hit without flushing the currently fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the decoded instruction without altering decoder legality or register operands.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare predicted next PC against the resolved branch/jump next PC, generate redirects only for misses or unpredicted transfers, and retain precise misalignment-trap behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and wire the predictor lookup/training path, coordinate predictor-hit and EX-mispredict control with existing flushes, and preserve RVFI retirement ordering.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\", \"category\"=>\"predictor\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>4, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Implement the one-entry fully tagged last-target buffer, including exact-PC lookup, taken-transfer training, matching not-taken invalidation, and reset state.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Give fetch a predicted target input with imemReady and EX-redirect priority, advancing on a valid predictor hit without flushing the currently fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the decoded instruction without altering decoder legality or register operands.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Compare predicted next PC against the resolved branch/jump next PC, generate redirects only for misses or unpredicted transfers, and retain precise misalignment-trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Instantiate and wire the predictor lookup/training path, coordinate predictor-hit and EX-mispredict control with existing flushes, and preserve RVFI retirement ordering.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
