 (rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:19.24-19.34): 8\\nSBY 17:52:54 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:07  Assert failed in rvfi_testbench: rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 (_witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_55)\\nSBY 17:52:54 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:07  Writing trace to VCD file: engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 17:52:54 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:08  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 17:52:54 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:08  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 17:52:54 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:08  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 17:52:54 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:08  Status: failed\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:08 (8)\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:04 (4)\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: pc_fwd_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_55 at rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 step 20\\nSBY 17:52:55 [pc_fwd_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1/formal/last_run-44716.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-44716/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (broken, n/a): ID-stage branch and jump redirects must latch resolved next-PC and misalignment-trap metadata with the instruction through ID/EX to retirement, because advancing fetch without keeping RVFI `pc_wdata` aligned can fail `pc_fwd` even when instruction checks pass.\"}\n10:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Decode-stage return-address stack predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark performs frequent function calls and returns, while the current\\ncore resolves JAL/JALR in EX and pays a redirect flush on every return.\\nEarlier IF-stage BTFNT and BTB attempts either lengthened the fetch path or\\nbroke pc_fwd, so a predictor should target the high-value JALR-return case\\nwithout adding instruction decode and target arithmetic to IF.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark performs frequent function calls and returns, while the current\\ncore resolves JAL/JALR in EX and pays a redirect flush on every return.\\nEarlier IF-stage BTFNT and BTB attempts either lengthened the fetch path or\\nbroke pc_fwd, so a predictor should target the high-value JALR-return case\\nwithout adding instruction decode and target arithmetic to IF.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small speculative return-address stack and perform return prediction\\nin ID for canonical JALR returns (x1/x5 link register, zero immediate).\\nTrack call pushes and return pops with a shadow/speculative stack, carry an\\nexplicit predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid bit through the pipeline,\\nand compare the prediction with EX's resolved next PC. On a mismatch, EX\\nmust redirect and restore the stack metadata so RVFI pc_wdata, ordering,\\ntraps, and arbitrary symbolic instruction streams remain precise. Keeping\\nthe lookup in ID confines the added muxing to the existing decode path while\\nremoving return redirect bubbles on repeated CoreMark call sites.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and return-stack action metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize canonical calls and returns, query the small return-address stack in decode, and pipeline prediction metadata without changing the architectural decode legality defaults.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept an early decode-stage predicted target with correct priority relative to reset, bus stalls, and EX recovery redirects, while retaining sequential fetch when the stack has no valid entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the carried return prediction against the resolved JAL/JALR next PC, generate precise recovery redirects, and expose committed call/return outcomes for stack repair.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode prediction and resolved recovery/training signals through the pipeline so only correctly predicted returns avoid the existing EX redirect flush.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC, prediction-valid, and return-stack action metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize canonical calls and returns, query the small return-address stack in decode, and pipeline prediction metadata without changing the architectural decode legality defaults.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept an early decode-stage predicted target with correct priority relative to reset, bus stalls, and EX recovery redirects, while retaining sequential fetch when the stack has no valid entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the carried return prediction against the resolved JAL/JALR next PC, generate precise recovery redirects, and expose committed call/return outcomes for stack repair.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire decode prediction and 