{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]).slice(\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Confidence-qualified tiny tagged BTB\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark still pays the EX redirect penalty on repeated control transfers,\n  but prior BTFNT and RAS predictors added fetch or decode critical-path cost,\n  while the last-target attempt failed because prediction metadata was not kept\n  precise through recovery. A small target-only structure can address the hot\n  loop case without decoding imemData in IF or maintaining a speculative stack.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a two-entry fully tagged branch-target buffer with a two-bit confidence\n  counter. Lookups use only the current fetch PC and registered tag/target\n  state, and predictions are enabled only for entries trained taken repeatedly;\n  EX trains taken branches and jumps, decays confidence on conditional exits,\n  and retains exact resolved-next-PC comparison. Carry predicted-valid and\n  predicted-next-PC fields atomically through IF/ID and ID/EX so a hit retires\n  with the correct RVFI pc_wdata, while every miss or exit flushes and repairs\n  the fetch PC precisely. This targets recurring CoreMark loop redirects while\n  limiting aliasing, wrong-path churn, and IF critical-path logic.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so prediction, mismatch recovery, and RVFI pc_wdata remain tied to the owning instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a two-entry fully tagged target buffer with confidence-qualified lookup, taken training, conditional-not-taken decay, and reset-safe replacement.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select a registered BTB target from the fetch PC without decoding imemData, preserve imemReady and redirect priority, and emit atomic prediction metadata with each fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the instruction and decoded control state.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute the resolved next PC, compare it with the carried prediction, generate redirects only on misses, and preserve misalignment-trap and precise pc_next behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire BTB lookup/training and prediction-aware flush control through the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the RVFI contract.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\", \"category\"=>\"predictor\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>4, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
