X recovery redirects, while retaining sequential fetch when the stack has no valid entry.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the carried return prediction against the resolved JAL/JALR next PC, generate precise recovery redirects, and expose committed call/return outcomes for stack repair.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire decode prediction and resolved recovery/training signals through the pipeline so only correctly predicted returns avoid the existing EX redirect flush.\"}]}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\",\"title\":\"Tiny fully tagged last-target predictor\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"cycles\":null,\"lesson\":null,\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so prediction and recovery remain tied to the instruction that made the lookup.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the one-entry fully tagged last-target buffer, including exact-PC lookup, taken-transfer training, matching not-taken invalidation, and reset state.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Give fetch a predicted target input with imemReady and EX-redirect priority, advancing on a valid predictor hit without flushing the currently fetched instruction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the decoded instruction without altering decoder legality or register operands.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare predicted next PC against the resolved branch/jump next PC, generate redirects only for misses or unpredicted transfers, and retain precise misalignment-trap behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Instantiate and wire the predictor lookup/training path, coordinate predictor-hit and EX-mispredict control with existing flushes, and preserve RVFI retirement 