{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The prior predictor sweep rules out broad BTFNT, RAS, tagged BTBs, and even a one-entry learned target table: their IF/EX metadata and recovery logic cost more than they save. The narrowest remaining opportunity is a zero-state, always-correct predictor for aligned unconditional `JAL` targets, avoiding conditional-outcome state and target-table lookup overhead while removing the common JAL flush."}}
