{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Aligned JAL early-target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage core resolves every JAL in EX, so an unconditional call or\n  jump flushes the sequentially fetched instructions even though its target\n  is fully encoded in the instruction and is always taken. Prior BTFNT and\n  learned BTB designs paid broad lookup, target, and recovery overhead across\n  the whole fetch stream; CoreMark should benefit more from a narrowly scoped\n  predictor that does not add conditional-history or replacement state.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a zero-state static predictor that recognizes only aligned RV32I JAL\n  instructions in IF, forms the J-immediate target, and fetches that target on\n  the following cycle. Carry only a one-bit predicted-JAL token with the\n  instruction; EX suppresses its normal JAL redirect only when that token is\n  present and the resolved target is aligned and agrees, while unpredicted or\n  misaligned JALs retain the existing precise redirect/trap path. Restricting\n  the fetch decode to opcode 1101111 avoids branch-history tables, JALR\n  speculation, and a general BTB, aiming to remove call/jump flushes with a\n  smaller Fmax and control penalty than earlier predictor attempts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a single predicted-JAL token to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles without carrying a target address through the pipeline.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize only aligned JAL opcodes, form the J-immediate target, select it for the next fetch, and emit the atomic prediction token while preserving redirect, stall, and reset priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pipeline the predicted-JAL token with the instruction and decoded operands so it remains tied to the owning JAL.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare tokenized JAL prediction against the resolved jump target and suppress only agreeing aligned redirects; preserve precise recovery and misalignment-trap behavior otherwise.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the prediction token through the existing front-end flush and EX redirect control without changing the single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
