{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"predictor\\\") | \\\"\\\\n--- \\\" + .id + \\\" ---\\\\n\\\" + .hypothesis.hypothesis + \\\"\\\\nchanges: \\\" + ([.changes[].file] | join(\\\", \\\"))' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"\n--- hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 ---\nAdd a low-area static BTFNT predictor in IF: recognize conditional branch\nopcodes from the fetched instruction, predict negative-offset branches taken,\nand form their immediate target during fetch. Carry prediction metadata with\nthe instruction and make EX redirect only when the predicted next PC differs\nfrom the resolved next PC, including the predicted-taken/actually-not-taken\nloop-exit case. This should remove most taken-loop bubbles without adding\npredictor state or weakening architectural recovery and RVFI behavior.\n\nchanges: rtl/core_pkg.sv, rtl/if_stage.sv, rtl/id_stage.sv, rtl/ex_stage.sv, rtl/core.sv\n\n--- hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 ---\nAdd a tiny direct-mapped BTB with PC tags, cached branch targets, and a\ntwo-bit taken counter. A tagged hit in IF predicts the cached target using\nonly the current PC, keeping opcode/funct/immediate decode out of the IF\ncritical path. Carry the predicted next PC with the instruction; in EX,\ncompare it with the resolved branch next PC and redirect only on a\nmisprediction. Train the BTB from resolved conditional branches, saturating\ntoward taken or not-taken, while retaining precise flush, trap, RVFI, and\nload/store stall behavior. This should remove repeated taken-loop redirect\nbubbles without repeating the timing-costly fetch-time BTFNT logic.\n\nchanges: rtl/core_pkg.sv, rtl/if_stage.sv, rtl/id_stage.sv, rtl/ex_stage.sv, rtl/core.sv\n\n--- hyp-20260710-003-r3s2 ---\nAdd a small speculative return-address stack and perform return prediction\nin ID for canonical JALR returns (x1/x5 link register, zero immediate).\nTrack call pushes and return pops with a shadow/speculative stack, carry an\nexplicit predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid bit through the pipeline,\nand compare the prediction with EX's resolved next PC. On a mismatch, EX\nmust redirect and restore the stack metadata so RVFI pc_wdata, ordering,\ntraps, and arbitrary symbolic instruction streams remain precise. Keeping\nthe lookup in ID confines the added muxing to the existing decode path while\nremoving return redirect bubbles on repeated CoreMark call sites.\n\nchanges: rtl/core_pkg.sv, rtl/id_stage.sv, rtl/if_stage.sv, rtl/ex_stage.sv, rtl/core.sv\n\n--- hyp-20260710-003-r4s2 ---\nAdd a one-entry last-target branch buffer indexed by an exact full-PC tag.\nOn a hit, fetch advances directly to the recorded target while the\ncurrent instruction carries prediction-valid and predicted-next-PC bits\nthrough ID/EX. Train the entry only from a valid EX-resolved taken branch,\nJAL, or JALR; invalidate it when a matching conditional branch resolves\nnot-taken. EX compares the carried prediction with the resolved next PC,\nsuppressing the normal redirect on a hit and redirecting plus flushing on\nevery miss. This preserves precise RVFI pc_wdata and recovery while\navoiding fetch-time opcode/immediate decode and limiting predictor muxing\nto one tag compare and target mux.\n\nchanges: rtl/core_pkg.sv, rtl/branch_predictor.sv, rtl/if_stage.sv, rtl/id_stage.sv, rtl/ex_stage.sv, rtl/core.sv\n\n--- hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 ---\nAdd a two-entry fully tagged branch-target buffer with a two-bit confidence\ncounter. Lookups use only the current fetch PC and registered tag/target\nstate, and predictions are enabled only for entries trained taken repeatedly;\nEX trains taken branches and jumps, decays confidence on conditional exits,\nand retains exact resolved-next-PC comparison. Carry predicted-valid and\npredicted-next-PC fields atomically through IF/ID and ID/EX so a hit retires\nwith the correct RVFI pc_wdata, while every miss or exit flushes and repairs\nthe fetch PC precisely. This targets recurring CoreMark loop redirects while\nlimiting aliasing, wrong-path churn, and IF critical-path logic.\n\nchanges: rtl/core_pkg.sv, rtl/branch_predictor.sv, rtl/if_stage.sv, rtl/id_stage.sv, rtl/ex_stage.sv, rtl/core.sv\n\n--- hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 ---\nAdd a one-entry exact-PC last-target predictor specialized for recurring\ncontrol-transfer PCs. IF uses the registered tag/target hit to fetch the\npredicted target, but carries only a one-bit prediction token with the\ninstruction; EX re-looks up the target and compares it with the resolved\nnext PC. A token is trusted only when the EX lookup still hits and agrees,\nso table replacement, not-taken exits, misaligned targets, and aliases\nalways take the normal precise redirect path. Train only on valid taken\nbranches and jumps, keeping the target mux and pipeline sideband smaller\nthan the prior metadata-heavy BTBs while removing steady-state loop flushes.\n\nchanges: rtl/core_pkg.sv, rtl/branch_predictor.sv, rtl/if_stage.sv, rtl/id_stage.sv, rtl/ex_stage.sv, rtl/core.sv\n\n--- hyp-20260710-003-r7s2 ---\nAdd a zero-state static predictor that recognizes only aligned RV32I JAL\ninstructions in IF, forms the J-immediate target, and fetches that target on\nthe following cycle. Carry only a one-bit predicted-JAL token with the\ninstruction; EX suppresses its normal JAL redirect only when that token is\npresent and the resolved target is aligned and agrees, while unpredicted or\nmisaligned JALs retain the existing precise redirect/trap path. Restricting\nthe fetch decode to opcode 1101111 avoids branch-history tables, JALR\nspeculation, and a general BTB, aiming to remove call/jump flushes with a\nsmaller Fmax and control penalty than earlier predictor attempts.\n\nchanges: rtl/core_pkg.sv, rtl/if_stage.sv, rtl/id_stage.sv, rtl/ex_stage.sv, rtl/core.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
