{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r8s2.yaml && test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r8s2.yaml && echo 'hypothesis file present'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\ntitle: \"Retirement-trained loop target cache\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictors either put branch decode and target arithmetic on the IF\n  critical path or carried broad prediction state through every pipeline\n  stage. The exact-PC target attempt was close to neutral, suggesting that\n  the useful signal is recurring taken loops, but the predictor must be\n  narrower and must not be polluted by calls, returns, or speculative\n  wrong-path training.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny direct-mapped loop-target cache trained only when a backward\n  conditional branch retires. Each entry stores an exact PC tag, its resolved\n  target, and an armed bit; IF uses a registered tag/target hit to redirect\n  only recurring loop branches. Carry only a compact cache-slot token with\n  the instruction, and protect the matching entry until EX resolves it so\n  table replacement cannot make an old prediction appear correct. A taken\n  hit suppresses the normal EX redirect, while a loop exit invalidates the\n  entry and follows the existing precise redirect path. Training at\n  retirement prevents wrong-path branches from changing predictor state and\n  the loop-only scope avoids adding JAL/JALR traffic to the hot predictor.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact loop-prediction token and validity fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles without carrying a 32-bit predicted target.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a small exact-PC loop-target cache with retirement training, armed/invalidation state, IF lookup, EX agreement lookup, and protection for an in-flight prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use only a loop-cache hit to select the next fetch PC, preserving imem stalls, redirect priority, and atomic prediction-token generation.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Pipeline the compact loop-cache token with the owning instruction and preserve flush/stall behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress redirects only for an armed loop-cache token whose resolved taken target agrees; retain precise recovery and misalignment traps for exits and misses.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect IF/EX predictor lookups and retirement-only training while keeping the single-issue RVFI contract and monotonic retirement unchanged.\"\nhypothesis file present\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
