{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short; git diff --stat; sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv        |   6 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv |  29 ++---\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv   | 271 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------\n 3 files changed, 214 insertions(+), 92 deletions(-)\n# Integrated direct-mapped data cache\n\nImplemented the cache at the MEM boundary in `rtl/mem_stage.sv` and wired\nits transaction-completion signal through `rtl/core.sv` into\n`rtl/hazard_unit.sv`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a reset-invalidated 2 KiB direct-mapped cache: 128 lines, four 32-bit\n  words per line, 21-bit tags.\n- Aligned loads in the normal `[0, 0x00100000)` RAM window hit locally.\n- Load misses hold the EX/MEM request and refill all four words through a\n  ready-aware serialized FSM before producing one MEM/WB response.\n- Stores are no-write-allocate and write through externally; cache-hit stores\n  update only the selected byte lanes in the cached word.\n- UART/marker MMIO, OOB addresses, and misaligned accesses bypass the cache.\n  Misaligned accesses remain precise traps with no bus transaction.\n- Hazard control now consumes `cache_busy`, so a local hit does not stall on a\n  low external dmem-ready signal while misses and outstanding direct writes do.\n- RVFI continues to report one architectural access; refill beats are hidden.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The cache is integrated into `mem_stage.sv` rather than a separate\n  `data_cache.sv` module, avoiding an additional source-list dependency.\n- The repository's formal runner could not execute in this sandbox: its\n  shared `formal/riscv-formal` symlink points outside the writable worktree,\n  and cleanup/staging failed with `Operation not permitted` before RTL\n  checks ran.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- `make lint TARGET=bench`: pass.\n- `make test TARGET=bench`: 5/5 pass.\n- Yosys Gowin synthesis with `core_bench_si.sv`: pass, zero structural\n  problems.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass for selftest and CoreMark.\n- Randomized CoreMark run with `--istall --dstall --seed 1`: completed with\n  `oob:false`, benchmark markers, and the evaluator's canonical CRCs\n  `crclist=0xe714`, `crcmatrix=0x1fd7`, `crcstate=0x8e3a`.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: blocked\n  by the sandbox permission failure above; no formal counterexample was\n  produced.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
