so a synthesized barrel-shifter-style cone may limit Fmax even\\nthough only four byte lanes are legal.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the variable load shift with an explicit four-way byte-lane mux and\\na two-way halfword-lane mux, and derive the byte masks from constant lookup\\ncases. Keep word loads, sign/zero extension, misalignment traps, dmem\\nhandshaking, and all RVFI memory fields unchanged. The narrower constant\\nlane network should reduce LUT depth and routing on the load-to-writeback\\npath without changing instruction timing or retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement explicit address-indexed load lane muxes and constant byte-mask cases, preserving exact RV32I load semantics, traps, handshakes, and RVFI fields.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement explicit address-indexed load lane muxes and constant byte-mask cases, preserving exact RV32I load semantics, traps, handshakes, and RVFI fields.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 370.39, \"delta_pct\": -8.97, \"vs_baseline\": 30.96, \"fmax_mhz\": 166.36, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7488, \"ff\": 1858, \"seeds\": [165.84, 173.04, 166.36], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T21:29:22.464159Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r5s0 (regression, -8.97%): Replacing variable load shifts with explicit lane-case muxes did not pay off in CoreMark, showing that added MEM-stage selection and routing can outweigh the expected barrel-shifter savings when the existing shift is already synthesized efficiently.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:15:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed two-stage execute pipeline\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline places operand forwarding, a 32-bit ALU,\\nbranch comparison, and control-transfer target formation in one EX cycle.\\nThat wide fan-in and arithmetic cone is a likely remaining Fmax limiter\\nafter the fast-path ALU optimization, while the prior buffering attempts\\nshow that adding queues can cost more IPC than they recover.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline places operand forwarding, a 32-bit ALU,\\nbranch comparison, and control-transfer target formation in one EX cycle.\\nThat wide fan-in and arithmetic cone is a likely remaining Fmax limiter\\nafter the fast-path ALU optimization, while the prior buffering attempts\\nshow that adding queues can cost more IPC than they recover.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split EX into EX1 and EX2 with a pipeline register between operand\\nselection and execution. EX1 performs source-use-aware forwarding and\\ncaptures the resolved operands and control metadata; EX2 performs the ALU,\\nbranch compare/target calculation, and memory-address generation before the\\nexisting MEM boundary. Add explicit EX1/EX2 bypass priority and interlocks\\nfor the extra latency, and keep redirects, load-use behavior, dmem stalls,\\nand RVFI payloads tied to the same in-order instruction. The added stage\\nshould shorten the critical operand-to-result path enough to raise Fmax\\nwithout the area and ordering overhead of speculative queues.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle definitions with an EX1/EX2 execution payload carrying forwarded operands, control, and RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Restructure execute into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/branch/address EX2 stages, with precise redirect and misalignment-trap propagation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add freshest-writer bypass selection for the retimed EX1/EX2 boundary while preserving load suppression, x0 handling, and EX/MEM priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-cycle interlocks and flush/stall precedence required by the extra execute stage, including dmem backpressure and redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the retimed execute stages into MEM/WB, forwarding, hazard control, and RVFI retirement without changing the single-channel top-level contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the pipeline bundle definitions with an EX1/EX2 execution payload carrying forwarded operands, control, and RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Restructure execute into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/branch/address EX2 stages, with precise redirect and misalignment-trap propagation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add freshest-writer bypass selection for the retimed EX1/EX2 boundary while preserving load suppression, x0 handling, and EX/MEM priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-cycle interlocks and flush/stall precedence required by the extra execute stage, including dmem backpressure and redirect recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the retimed execute stages into MEM/WB, forwarding, hazard control, and RVFI retirement without changing the single-channel top-level contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 188.61, \"delta_pct\": -53.64, \"vs_baseline\": -33.31, \"fmax_mhz\": 102.76, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 5448270, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7636, \"ff\": 2112, \"seeds\": [88.33, 110.57, 102.76], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T21:43:14.515659Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -53.64%): Retiming EX into EX1/EX2 made dependency, redirect, and dmem-stall interlocks pay extra latency on common in-order paths, so CoreMark IPC loss overwhelmed any Fmax benefit; deeper pipelines need latency-aware bypassing without serializing ALU chains.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:16:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Confidence-qualified tiny tagged BTB\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark still pays the EX redirect penalty on repeated control transfers,\\nbut prior BTFNT and RAS predictors added fetch or decode critical-path cost,\\nwhile the last-target attempt failed because prediction metadata was not kept\\nprecise through recovery. A small target-only structure can address the hot\\nloop case without decoding imemData in IF or maintaining a speculative stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark still pays the EX redirect penalty on repeated control transfers,\\nbut prior BTFNT and RAS predictors added fetch or decode critical-path cost,\\nwhile the last-target attempt failed because prediction metadata was not kept\\nprecise through recovery. A small target-only structure can address the hot\\nloop case without decoding imemData in IF or maintaining a speculative stack.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a two-entry fully tagged branch-target buffer with a two-bit confidence\\ncounter. Lookups use only the current fetch PC and registered tag/target\\nstate, and predictions are enabled only for entries trained taken repeatedly;\\nEX trains taken branches and jumps, decays confidence on conditional exits,\\nand retains exact resolved-next-PC comparison. Carry predicted-valid and\\npredicted-next-PC fields atomically through IF/ID and ID/EX so a hit retires\\nwith the correct RVFI pc_wdata, while every miss or exit flushes and repairs\\nthe fetch PC precisely. This targets recurring CoreMark loop redirects while\\nlimiting aliasing, wrong-path churn, and IF critical-path logic.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so prediction, mismatch recovery, and RVFI pc_wdata remain tied to the owning instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a two-entry fully tagged target buffer with confidence-qualified lookup, taken training, conditional-not-taken decay, and reset-safe replacement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select a registered BTB target from the fetch PC without decoding imemData, preserve imemReady and redirect priority, and emit atomic prediction metadata with each fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the instruction and decoded control state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the resolved next PC, compare it with the carried prediction, generate redirects only on misses, and preserve misalignment-trap and precise pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire BTB lookup/training and prediction-aware flush control through the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so prediction, mismatch recovery, and RVFI pc_wdata remain tied to the owning instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a two-entry fully tagged target buffer with confidence-qualified lookup, taken training, conditional-not-taken decay, and reset-safe replacement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Select a registered BTB target from the fetch PC without decoding imemData, preserve imemReady and redirect priority, and emit atomic prediction metadata with each fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pipeline prediction metadata unchanged alongside the instruction and decoded control state.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute the resolved next PC, compare it with the carried prediction, generate redirects only on misses, and preserve misalignment-trap and precise pc_next behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire BTB lookup/training and prediction-aware flush control through the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 306.85, \"delta_pct\": -24.58, \"vs_baseline\": 8.5, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.05, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4303443, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7928, \"ff\": 2031, \"seeds\": [123.93, 132.05, 134.3], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T21:37:48.155196Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (regression, -24.58%): Even confidence-gating a two-entry tagged BTB can regress CoreMark when every fetched instruction carries `predicted_valid`/`predicted_next_pc` through ID/EX and pays IF next-PC selection plus EX resolved-next-PC comparison and flush-repair overhead for a small number of saved loop redirects.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:17:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Source-use-aware load-use interlock\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The load-use detector currently compares a load destination against both\\nrs1 and rs2 bit fields of every following instruction, even when that\\ninstruction does not read one or either field. Immediate, upper-immediate,\\njump, fence, and system encodings can therefore consume a needless bubble\\nin CoreMark. Removing these false hazards improves retired instructions per\\ncycle without changing the five-stage timing or the external bus contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The load-use detector currently compares a load destination against both\\nrs1 and rs2 bit fields of every following instruction, even when that\\ninstruction does not read one or either field. Immediate, upper-immediate,\\njump, fence, and system encodings can therefore consume a needless bubble\\nin CoreMark. Removing these false hazards improves retired instructions per\\ncycle without changing the five-stage timing or the external bus contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Derive precise source-use bits for the IF/ID instruction from the existing\\nlegal RV32IM decode and feed them into the hazard unit. Stall for load-use\\nonly when the load rd is nonzero and matches a genuinely read rs1 or rs2;\\npreserve the current one-cycle interlock for R-type, branch, store, and\\naddress-generating consumers, along with all redirect, dmem-stall, x0, trap,\\nand RVFI ordering behavior. This should eliminate false bubbles while\\nleaving the optimized ALU and the common execute datapath unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decode-derived use_rs1/use_rs2 signals for the current IF/ID instruction, asserting them only for valid RV32IM consumers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use comparisons with the source-use signals while retaining exact load, x0, redirect, instruction-stall, and data-stall precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the ID-stage source-use metadata into hazard detection without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose decode-derived use_rs1/use_rs2 signals for the current IF/ID instruction, asserting them only for valid RV32IM consumers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use comparisons with the source-use signals while retaining exact load, x0, redirect, instruction-stall, and data-stall precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the ID-stage source-use metadata into hazard detection without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\nime [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_sra_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_sra_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_sra_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Status: passed\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 18:51:33 [insn_srai_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: reg_ch0\\n\\n--- reg_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 18:51:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 11..\\nSBY 18:51:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 12..\\nSBY 18:51:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 13..\\nSBY 18:51:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 14..\\nSBY 18:51:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 15..\\nSBY 18:5