 fanout without adding\\nlatency, changing forwarding, or altering IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Factor the existing ALU M-operation and divide gating predicates into Boolean decode from the current operation encoding, preserving real RV32M and ALTOPS behavior while reducing common-path range-comparator logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Factor the existing ALU M-operation and divide gating predicates into Boolean decode from the current operation encoding, preserving real RV32M and ALTOPS behavior while reducing common-path range-comparator logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 179.41, \"delta_pct\": -55.91, \"vs_baseline\": -36.56, \"fmax_mhz\": 80.58, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 7470, \"ff\": 1858, \"seeds\": [78.57, 80.58, 84.6], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T22:50:37.257453Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r9s0 (regression, -55.91%): Bit-factoring M-operation and multiply/divide predicates can regress even as it removes relational compares, showing that decode Boolean simplification is not a proxy for a shorter synthesized control-to-result path or lower fanout.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:27:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Isolate divide/remainder in a multi-cycle unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current fast-path split protects ordinary ALU operations, but the\\ncombinational RV32M divide and remainder operators still synthesize into a\\nlarge variable-division cone in the execute stage. That cone can limit the\\nFPGA clock even when CoreMark spends most cycles on integer and address\\ngeneration work.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current fast-path split protects ordinary ALU operations, but the\\ncombinational RV32M divide and remainder operators still synthesize into a\\nlarge variable-division cone in the execute stage. That cone can limit the\\nFPGA clock even when CoreMark spends most cycles on integer and address\\ngeneration work.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU out of the combinational ALU into a dedicated\\niterative execute-side unit with a registered request, busy state, and\\nresult completion. Stall only the in-order pipeline while an M divide is\\nactive, forward the completed result through the existing writeback path,\\nand retain the exact RV32M divide-by-zero and signed-overflow semantics.\\nRemoving the / and % cones from the normal EX result path should raise Fmax;\\nthe extra latency should have limited CoreMark impact because divide and\\nremainder instructions are uncommon relative to the common integer path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU arithmetic from the common ALU result path and expose only the fast integer and multiply operations to EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the registered iterative divide/remainder execution state, completion result, and precise operand/control capture while preserving forwarding and misalignment/trap metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate a divide-unit busy/hold interlock that freezes younger instructions without duplicating or retiring the in-flight divide, while retaining existing load-use, redirect, and dmem-stall precedence.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire divide request, busy, and completion signals through the pipeline so DIV/REM retire once in order through the existing single RVFI channel.\"}]}, \"