{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The first wiring pass exposed an important boundary detail: a cacheable load miss must remain incomplete even when beat zero is accepted, otherwise EX/MEM would advance before the four-word refill finishes. That case is now explicitly held, with the line-base refill request driven during the idle miss cycle."}}
